{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide","id":978575,"title":"When Worlds of Darkness Collide!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-29T13:25:20-07:00","id":978575,"title":"When Worlds of Darkness Collide!","content":"(Notice the lack of &quot;vs&quot; in the title. This is NOT meant to be a &quot;fight thread&quot;, although if you all really WANT to debate such things, I'm game!)<br /> <br /> Opening Premise: Some sort of Wyld storm occurs, making the impossible happen. The two separate worlds of darkness mix and merge. As improbable as it sounds, this is a stable union, that somehow preserves cosmologies that would normally be considered incompatible (IOW, this is pure Handwavium, meant to preempt arguments that only one set of Mages' powers should work, etc, which would not be in the spirit of the thread's intent).<br /> <br /> How do you think the various Supernaturals would react on meeting their counterparts? Would Requiem Kindred and Cainites easily find common cause? Would Garou and Uratha recognize each other as werewolves? Could the Traditions fit the Pentacle into their Paradigm, and is the world big enough for the Seers and the Technocracy?<br /> <br /> From Mummies to Demons to Changelings, who has the most impact on the others' culture and how might they grow from here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:00:32-07:00","id":978602,"title":"","content":"Requiem vampires and Masquerade vampires would have some interesting opinions on what each other <i>are</i>, since the Masquerade Clans are a result of divergent &quot;evolution&quot; from a single progenitor and the Requiem Clans are (probably) a result of convergent &quot;evolution&quot; from a plethora of blood-drinking monsters. I could see Requiem vampires acknowledging Cainites as Kindred, though they might look at them all as a single, very diverse Clan with a lot of Bloodlines. But Cainites might not acknowledge Requiem vampires as true Kindred, since they aren't descendants of Caine. Also, what would the Strix think of Cainites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:03:39-07:00","id":978605,"title":"","content":"I think Masquerade vampires would likely run roughshod over Requiem vampires. It's a more power heavy game and, more importantly, a lot less localized. The Camarilla is much more focused on the Masquerade and deeply embedded not just in city but in regional and national politics. I imagine the Invictus would be pretty rapidly folded into the Camarilla and &quot;deviant&quot; covenants like the Circle of the Crone and the Carthians forced to pivot to their off foot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:10:29-07:00","id":978613,"title":"","content":"I think there is already another thread like this sitting around on the forum...<br /> <br /> Do you mean both meet in one big mash-up, or just how each deals with its analog (where possible)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:10:57-07:00","id":978614,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eaters and Wraiths would get along like a house on ethereal fire. Geists not as much, but given how they gave up some of themselves to <i>retain </i>their memories of being human, they'd probably just weird each other out.<br /> <br /> The two Changelings, the Lost would probably have their heads permanently cocked at the immature nutjobs who think Arcadia was a <i>good place. </i>On the other hand, the Kithain can and do show actual empathy, so they wouldn't be that adversarial. Maybe they'd even figure out how to stop the withering of the Fae Soul-the Hedge is anything but banal.<br /> <br /> The Fallen would have Yet Another Stupid Existential Crisis upon realizing God &quot;replaced&quot; them with a somewhat sentient supercomputer. With parts that are entirely sentient and flawed enough to wonder if they're doing the right thing and Fall on their own.<br /> <br /> Awakened and the Traditions...wouldn't really get along. They're based in completely opposite views of the world, Enlightenment vs. Romanticism. Some would get along a lot better (Euthanatos and Guardians, Free Council and Dreamspeakers/Society of Ether), but the others are just too alien. Seers and Technocrats? Even if there <i>was </i>room, the Union would still kill them on sight-they're everything wrong with Reality Deviants, and they do it with a <i>smile. </i>Naturally, the Union is blind to just how truly similar they are-but the Seers aren't. Nephandi would probably discover the hard way that Scelesti are less vile than they are as a general rule. A few might even find they, horrifyingly, <i>have had their Avatars healed</i>-the Abyss contains all impossibilities, including a way back from being one of the Dark's. Ability to deal with normal conscience not included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:11:37-07:00","id":978615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=978602#post978602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what would the Strix think of Cainites?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<i>Play toys!</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=978605#post978605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Masquerade vampires would likely run roughshod over Requiem vampires. It's a more power heavy game and, more importantly, a lot less localized. The Camarilla is much more focused on the Masquerade and deeply embedded not just in city but in regional and national politics. I imagine the Invictus would be pretty rapidly folded into the Camarilla and &quot;deviant&quot; covenants like the Circle of the Crone and the Carthians forced to pivot to their off foot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think over time though, Requiem vampires would take control, simply due to their Blood Potency increasing easier than Generation (as I understand the systems).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-29-2016, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:16:06-07:00","id":978618,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of more interested in WoD Changelings interacting with Beasts than with ChroD Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:43:29-07:00","id":978644,"title":"","content":"I assume that the Cainte would look at the Kindred like how the Kindred look at the Wicked Dead- something strange and terrifying which doesn't play by the rules. The Strixs would be, undoubtedly, be connected to the Dark Mother- and as such they may even claim that the Kindred are abominations made by Lilith as adversary to Cain's children (depends on how religious they are). If anything, I would imagine that the Cainte would try to close themselves from the All Night Society, seeing their practices and abilities as both familiar and strange. The Kindred, on the other hand, would have a lot less problem to accept the new vampires- they are more human than most of the Wicked Dead, after all, although they would not want to enter their mad political games and the Jihad their Blood Gods are playing.<br /> <br /> The Uratha would see the Gauro and the rest of the Fera with suspicion, as they see every other weird shapeshifter. They would think that Fomori, Drones, Gorgons and Kami are either forms of Hosts or Claimed, and perhaps even some of the Fera (like the werecrows). The Gauro may have a lot harsher view of the Uratha- while they are not tainted by either of the Triad, they are not the children of Gaia but bastards of the Moon Goddess and Wolf. Even further, they have destroyed their own Totem, which must have weakened the Emerald Mother, creating some grudge between them. The Pure may be more accepted among the Gauro, especially Lupus. We are talking about a group who once butchered their own kind- they'll have little qualms attacking the Forsaken, not to mention other shifters (the Unclean would probably be seen as Wyrm spawn). How do you mix the two spirit worlds together I don't know.<br /> <br /> Awakening and Ascension could work quit well together, since their cosmologies are quit different- Awakening Mages already accept that there are weird forms of magic in the world, while Ascension Mages would just claim the former to not practice True Magick but some variant using pacts and soul bindings with primordial beings. Dreaming and Lost Changelings would also work pretty well together as two separate cosmologies, although just try to explain a Lost that you are a faerie in human body without her trying to impale you on cold iron. The Dreaming may be tied to the Skein or the Primordial Dream, with the Kithian being &quot;neighbors&quot; of the Begotten. Reckoning and Vigil Hunters share nothing in common, with the former may treat the latter as &quot;supporting cast&quot; or potential threat (Cheiron would, undoubtedly, rip a Reckoning Hunter to shreds in order to make new taumatech). Geist, Orpheus and Wraith may work well together as each taking a different niche (ghosts, projectors and mediums), but like Werewolf, you'll have to solve the &quot;two Underworlds&quot; problem. Perhaps using the Lower Depths or some other layer of reality. The Arisen would undoubtedly claim the Amenti to be a form of Lifeless- broken souls of ancients who tried to mimic the Rite of Return, although they are not tainted by the Devourer. The Amenti, on the other hand, would see the former as ancient and terrible beings which carry the shadow of Apep, or perhaps reborn gods of the old. Anyway, they would recognize them as beings older than they are and, like anyone else in the setting, would do their best to stay way from them. The Fallen and the Unchained would also share little in common- the Fallen may think that the God Machine is a creation of Lucifer or one of his generals (or even an Earthbound by itself) which is used to rebel against God and cut away His/Her power. They would look down at the Unchained as &quot;mockery&quot; of both angels and demons. The Unchained, however, may have great interest in the Fallen as a tool to use against the Machine or some path to Hell. Of course, the Hell they come from may not be the Hell the other wish to live in. The Kui Jin would be another form of &quot;Wicked Dead&quot; for both the Cainte and the Kindred.<br /> <br /> And sad little Promethean is all alone, with no one to play with- everyone would hate them as usually, and the Fallen may be even more terrified from their qasmalim than anything else in the setting. The Fallen would also look down ion the demons of Inferno (taints of human sin and passion are nothing compared the true fallen angels, in their opinion). Gypsy and Changeing Breeds would become true soul mates, as no one else would like to play with them :P<br /> <br /> Hope anything of that has helped!<br /> <br /> (I'm a bit tired, so I may expand things a bit after some sleep)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 09-29-2016, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:56:34-07:00","id":978687,"title":"","content":"<b>Mage</b> and <b>Changeling</b> cosmologies are surprisingly complementary along the WoD/ChroD divide:<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening</b>'s mages would eventually end up referring to the two types as Supernal Mages (themselves) and Phenomenal Mages (their <b>Ascension</b> counterparts, who manipulate the <s>Fallen</s>Phenomenal world directly, without recourse to Supernal symbols). For their part, the <b>Ascension</b> mages would view their <b>Awakening</b> counterparts as a more splintered variant of the Order of Hermes. The Technocracy and the Seers would likely despise each other: to the Technocracy, the Seers are everything they fear and loathe about Superstitions; and to the Seers, the Union is a rival to their own Pantechnicon that shows no fealty to the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> You could merge the two versions of <b>Changeling</b> by treating them as flip sides of the same coin: where ChroD's changelings are humans who were abducted to Arcadia and eventually escaped after being changed by the ordeal, WoD's changelings are Fae who were exiled from Arcadia and forced to adapt to a hostile world. From the Lost perspective, that sounds an awful lot like a Charlatan\u2026<br /> <br /> That said, I'll reserve final judgment until CtL2e and CtD20 are both out: both promise significant changes from their respective prior editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-30-2016, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T16:32:43-07:00","id":978706,"title":"","content":"I think it's safe to presume that the two Hunter lines are gonna have a bitch of a time figuring out if they can work with the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T16:37:55-07:00","id":978710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=978706#post978706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's safe to presume that the two Hunter lines are gonna have a bitch of a time figuring out if they can work with the other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think, to Vigil hunters, the powers of the Reckoning hunters will look suspiciously like the kinds manifested by slashers. The Lucifuge, MM, and Long Night would probably have some interesting thoughts about the &quot;higher powers&quot; they talk to. That said, I don't think they'd make too big of waves. The CoD is already a strange and scary place with plenty of inexplicable phenomena. What would probably be more worrying to the major compacts and covenants would be how these various groups of supernaturals suddenly seem capable of and encouraged to organize in large and largely functioning organizations that span well beyond the confines of individual cities or territorial regions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T19:17:16-07:00","id":978783,"title":"","content":"Mages would just <i>adapt</i> and add the new factions to their catalogue. Technocracy would just add new ones to control.<br /> <br /> Fallen would suffer imo: Their usual &quot;yeah, but the actual truth is that God [insert]' wouldn't hold much for creatures from another world. While no one would <i>know for sure</i> anything about these other beings and their original world, that would be a first for the Fallen, specially because of this machine demiurge. Unchained on the other hand would shrug and say something along the lines of &quot;New kind of angel. Everybody lay low until further notice&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T23:11:48-07:00","id":978882,"title":"","content":"After some sleep and some more thoughts- I think that the Kuei Jin could actually work by replacing the Thousand Hells with the Lower Depths- that is, people who died while being influenced and devoured by one of the Depths yet escaped, and now the hole in their soul requires to be filled with the souls of other. As for Reckoning Hunters, I won't be surprised if the Unchained would claim them to be slaves of the God Machine as some &quot;high form&quot; of Stigmatics. While Wraiths could be tied to the regular Underworld, the dead empires of the Dark Kingdoms and the sleeping Neverborn at the Labyrinth are cool concepts, which I think deserve their own &quot;plain of existence&quot;- maybe we could tie it to some sort of &quot;deep Twilight&quot; in which ghosts manipulate ephemera into creating complex structures and sailing into places beyond the world. Still stuck about how to mix Umbra and the Shadow and still keeping each distinct flavor, or how to justify having two different spirit realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T03:46:44-07:00","id":978941,"title":"","content":"The OWOD tends to have more ordered, rigid structures, that I think don't would not be as adaptive as the CoD.<br /> <br /> And too many people in the CoD know at least something about the Supernatural.<br /> <br /> So the Carmilla would likely crack like a nut, too much unpredictable shit going on, too many new threats, too many breaches in the Masqerade, too many new ideas, too many rivals.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy would be even worse off, they wouldn't have the same influence and control over consentual reality. Both Seers and Pentacle are capable of setting aside mutual hate for a common goal when absolutely needed, so I can see a three way alliance against the Technocracies attempts at control, perhaps toppling it entirely.<br /> <br /> The werewolves would be fighting for territory, but ultimately the Garou would also be fighting Industry Spirits, which would be too many enemies and they'd be driven from the cities entirely.<br /> <br /> Changelings from Lost would opened up gateways to the Hedge, perhaps on major Trods like Young street, and you'd never see the Dreaming Changelings again.<br /> <br /> So once the dust settled Technocracy, Garou, Cainites, Dreaming Changelings would be largely crushed, on the run, or gone entirely.<br /> <br /> Of the OWOD major splats the Acendancy Mages would be the only major power left, vying for power with rivals mages. Some surviving Cainites might get absorbed by the Reqiuem Kindred as perhaps a new clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:22:52-07:00","id":978958,"title":"","content":"The question is- why should such war happen? There are already dozens of different organizations, groups and cults in the setting, and most of the splats can't even agree with one another about what to eat for breakfast, not to mention destroying another supernatural. If anything, the &quot;unified splatism&quot; mentality of creatures from the CWoD would be on their side, in case such struggle would happen (which may not even be required).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:09:52-07:00","id":979029,"title":"","content":"What I'm really wondering is how the Tremere would react to the Ordo Dracul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:24:10-07:00","id":979037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=979029#post979029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm really wondering is how the Tremere would react to the Ordo Dracul.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing's for certain, they would be incredibly jealous of Chronicles' Tremere, who have all the abilities of mage and none of the weaknesses of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-30-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:38:29-07:00","id":979055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=979029#post979029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm really wondering is how the Tremere would react to the Ordo Dracul.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the tremere and ordo dracul would get along famously. They're both occultist groups who want to gain more power than what they are normally able to gather. The ordo dracul go about it by changing themselves and how their vampirism works, the tremere do it by utilizing blood sorceries. Both of them have a similar goal and a lot to teach each other... if they can get over the natural paranoia that comes with being a member of their group. What'd probably happen is they'd just compete for recruits and resources and wind up in a serious magical war that the elders of the tremere would try and win by major thaumaturgical rituals and the elders of the ordo dracul would argue with each other about how to fight and wind up doing mostly ineffective city focused efforts (the problem you get with more city focused groups vs an internationally organised one with a central leadership that has the literal blood bound devotion of all the members is that the internationally focused one has far more power and resources to muster overall).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:49:39-07:00","id":979073,"title":"","content":"Going with all the groups as written you'd either see a lot of uncharacteristic nationally organised movements in the CoD or any conflict with the CoD group vs the WoD group winding up in the WoD group's favour, purely because of the national focus and resources. In the long term the CoD would wind up with national level organisation and resources, but assuming the default city based start that I always prefer the CoD groups would have a hard time surviving against the nationally focused ones from WoD. The exception would be the mage groups where the orders already are a more nationally scaled group already who can organise relatively easily against a major threat like the technocrats or the traditions if the traditions somehow decided to go against the orders (which is unlikely as the orders fit decently with the traditions I think, at least as allies, if not full members).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:04:52-07:00","id":979087,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I don't think the &quot;ChroD has a local focus&quot; holds up beyond like... 1e Requiem. Tier scaling has been a consideration since Vigil, and pretty much every line is fully capable of operating at any Tier in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:31:05-07:00","id":979106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=979087#post979087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I don't think the &quot;ChroD has a local focus&quot; holds up beyond like... 1e Requiem. Tier scaling has been a consideration since Vigil, and pretty much every line is fully capable of operating at any Tier in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Really it comes down to your own personal preference when it comes to 2e. I personally run the mage orders, the lancea et sanctum, the ordo dracul and some aspects of the invictus as worldwide focus with some of the other groups as being international depending on my chronicle (like werewolves being internationaly but almost only when it comes to tribal pillar lodges), but for the most part there isn't much international organisation outside of those groups. Though I have friends who run everything they do as exclusively citywide and others who try to make every single splat internationally focused (even when using 2ed changeling preview court rules).<br /> <br /> So I guess it comes down to how you typically run your CoD lines when you compare them to the WoD ones. I usually think on what makes the most sense when it is expanded, so the circle of the crone would wind up a bunch of disparate groups that don't care about each other but the lancea would probably wind up appointing their own version of the pope who is the closest to an overlord ruler that the lancea have and the werewolf tribes in my vision typically don't care about other members except their own pack and for the rare regional gathering (would say moot but that brings up very different imagery for me, usually involving a lot of shaking, a judge and being horribly prepared for the situation). I will say outside of vampires, werewolves and mages (and hunters) I don't see anything but city level groups making any sense with the setting and rules as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:24:32-07:00","id":980062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=978602#post978602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requiem vampires and Masquerade vampires would have some interesting opinions on what each other <i>are</i>, since the Masquerade Clans are a result of divergent &quot;evolution&quot; from a single progenitor and the Requiem Clans are (probably) a result of convergent &quot;evolution&quot; from a plethora of blood-drinking monsters. I could see Requiem vampires acknowledging Cainites as Kindred, though they might look at them all as a single, very diverse Clan with a lot of Bloodlines. But Cainites might not acknowledge Requiem vampires as true Kindred, since they aren't descendants of Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there really any &quot;biological&quot; evidence to back any of that up, tho? Of all the supernaturals, vampires changed the least, so either might be able to pass as the other...except that thing Requiem vamps have where the Beast does a Quickening when two vamps meet. But since Masquerade vamps also have the Beast, theirs would probably adjust to that quickly...<br /> <br /> Comparing notes would be interesting, esp. with Cainites learning that the All Night Society created the Camarilla *much* earlier in history, but that it fell apart long ago...There would also be plenty of &quot;No, WE'RE the TRUE Ventrue!&quot; going around, I'm sure...otoh, Cainites would probably say, &quot;Wait, you guys don't have to deal with ANY Malkavians?? Lucky...&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Werewolves would be interesting, as there's so much similar, yet with little differences, like how they have the SAME Auspices, with the same pack roles and everything, just with...different names, for some reason. Those differences in First Tongue would throw everyone off, and the Spirits would just be hopelessly confused! I'd like to see how a meeting between Storm Lords with Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords would go down...poorly, I expect. OTOH, I think the Iron Masters would get on famously with the Glass Walkers, and they might even negotiate some sort of Tribal Merger!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two Changelings, the Lost would probably have their heads permanently cocked at the immature nutjobs who think Arcadia was a <i>good place. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know whether to laugh or cry at the thought of Kithain charging through the Hedge, loudly announcing themselves to the Fae, &quot;Here we are! We're HOME! We're...oh, shiiiit!!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kind of more interested in WoD Changelings interacting with Beasts than with ChroD Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, they would be tied into the Dreaming somehow! CtD gave us some pc types who weren't Fae, but were related to them, like the Denizens of the Dreaming (anyone remember that supplement? did those guys ever show up again, like, anywhere?); Beasts would probably be recognized as such distant relatives...Could that mean that Kithain's mucking about in the Dreaming could also create Heroes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And sad little Promethean is all alone, with no one to play with-</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a little known fact, but Prommies DID, in fact, first pop up in the CWoD...in one book only, in an attempt to drum up interest for an eventual gameline, which sadly had to wait for a new WoD to get greenlit. I have the book they showed up in, but it makes for a great trivia question, so...does anyone else know what book they were in?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 10-02-2016, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T06:07:55-07:00","id":980208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=980062#post980062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there really any &amp;quot;biological&amp;quot; evidence to back any of that up, tho? Of all the supernaturals, vampires changed the least, so either might be able to pass as the other...except that thing Requiem vamps have where the Beast does a Quickening when two vamps meet. But since Masquerade vamps also have the Beast, theirs would probably adjust to that quickly...<br /> <br /> Comparing notes would be interesting, esp. with Cainites learning that the All Night Society created the Camarilla *much* earlier in history, but that it fell apart long ago...There would also be plenty of &amp;quot;No, WE'RE the TRUE Ventrue!&amp;quot; going around, I'm sure...otoh, Cainites would probably say, &amp;quot;Wait, you guys don't have to deal with ANY Malkavians?? Lucky...&amp;quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Werewolves would be interesting, as there's so much similar, yet with little differences, like how they have the SAME Auspices, with the same pack roles and everything, just with...different names, for some reason. Those differences in First Tongue would throw everyone off, and the Spirits would just be hopelessly confused! I'd like to see how a meeting between Storm Lords with Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords would go down...poorly, I expect. OTOH, I think the Iron Masters would get on famously with the Glass Walkers, and they might even negotiate some sort of Tribal Merger!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know whether to laugh or cry at the thought of Kithain charging through the Hedge, loudly announcing themselves to the Fae, &amp;quot;Here we are! We're HOME! We're...oh, shiiiit!!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Good point, they would be tied into the Dreaming somehow! CtD gave us some pc types who weren't Fae, but were related to them, like the Denizens of the Dreaming (anyone remember that supplement? did those guys ever show up again, like, anywhere?); Beasts would probably be recognized as such distant relatives...Could that mean that Kithain's mucking about in the Dreaming could also create Heroes?<br /> <br /> <br /> It's a little known fact, but Prommies DID, in fact, first pop up in the CWoD...in one book only, in an attempt to drum up interest for an eventual gameline, which sadly had to wait for a new WoD to get greenlit. I have the book they showed up in, but it makes for a great trivia question, so...does anyone else know what book they were in?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Wbat book did Prommies appear in in OWOD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T06:39:36-07:00","id":980218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=980208#post980208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wbat book did Prommies appear in in OWOD?</div> </div> </div> </div>Storyteller's Handbook, p.154","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:00:45-07:00","id":980240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=980218#post980218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storyteller's Handbook, p.154</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically, Mage Revised's Storyteller's Handbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:51:50-07:00","id":981750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=980240#post980240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Specifically, Mage Revised's Storyteller's Handbook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'll be killed and reanimated. I didn't know that. Kind of funny that there wasn't any interest then, considering how staunch Promethean fans are now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T12:50:55-07:00","id":982276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=978941#post978941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy would be even worse off, they wouldn't have the same influence and control over consentual reality. Both Seers and Pentacle are capable of setting aside mutual hate for a common goal when absolutely needed, so I can see a three way alliance against the Technocracies attempts at control, perhaps toppling it entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is untrue. The Technocracy and the Traditions made an alliance during WWII against the Nephandi which was very successful, and the Technocracy has far greater reach and grasp than the Seers ever had.<br /> <br /> What's far more likely is that the Union establishes a truce with the Pentacle because the Union isn't made of idiots, and they can easily see that going into a three-way war is a pretty stupid idea.<br /> <br /> Besides, the Pentacle seems totally reasonable compared to the Traditions in the eyes of the Union. Where the Union gets to fight against the Order of Hermes, the Seers get to fight against the Silver Ladder who are staunch humanists wishing to see mankind stand ascendant over all gods and all oppression, who freely acknowledge the beauty of science and technology. <hr />High ranking Technocrat: &quot;Hey those Silver Ladder guys seem pretty reasonable, way better than our own Reality Deviants, we should enter a non-aggression pact and not try to fuck them over because a three-way war is a pretty bad idea.&quot;<br /> <br /> Other high ranking Technocrat: &quot;Yeah, maybe launch some propaganda campaigns about how awesome the Union is.&quot;<br /> <br /> High ranking Technocrat: &quot;Those Seer guys seem like assholes though.&quot;<br /> <br /> Other high ranking Technocrat: &quot;They are <i>literally</i> every stereotype about the superstitionists that the Order of Reason fought against, including the whole &quot;barons taxing the night&quot; part.&quot;<br /> <br /> High ranking Technocrat: &quot;Do you think we can go into an alliance of convenience with the Pentacle against them?&quot;<br /> <br /> Other high ranking Technocrat: &quot;It might be up for consideration yes.&quot; <hr /><br /> Like, yes the Technocracy represents a lot of bad stuff (I won't ever claim that the Technocracy is an unambiguous force for good,, even though they're my favorite faction), but at the same time, they'll look <i>really sympathetic</i> if you're a Silver Ladder mage or Guardian of The Veil for that sake.<br /> <br /> Their symbolism is all about being the guardians in the shadows and the people who give of themselves so humanity can prosper, sure they use some pretty ugly methods, but it's not like the Orders are innocent lambs either.<br /> <br /> What I think is way more interesting than this however, is the meeting between Technocrats and Demons.<br /> <br /> Do you know what the God-Machine looks like to me? It looks like the Computer.<br /> <br /> Iteration X's artificial God, created in the image of man to be a worthy deity (that is really possessed by a Spirit).<br /> <br /> I can quickly see a schism forming in the Union, with the Iterators wanting to aid the Machine, the Syndicate wanting some Demons on the payroll, the Void Engineers wanting Demon allies and the NWO staying neutral with the Progenitors, though they'll probably be on the more conservative side both of them.<br /> <br /> Changelings however, get full on sympathy and aid from the Technocracy, they're literally normal people who have been kidnapped by malevolent EDEs and xenografted with a bunch of nasty stuff. The Union would want to recruit the shit out of that, and help them with their situation, not only does it get them a bunch of allies of convenience, but it also gives them access to a bunch of really good at being subtle people with neat powers and a really good ability to get out of any situation.<br /> <br /> Their powers are easily explained as xenografts anyway.<br /> <br /> Now I'll go and write a bunch of Changelings who work for the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":6042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","user":"ManusDomine","date":". 10-06-2016, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:44:14-07:00","id":982318,"title":"","content":"I think what'd be interesting is how some groups would draw parallels between cosmic entities. WoD folks would probably peg the G-M as an aspect of the Weaver, Ammut and the Flux portion of the Divine Fire as the Wyrm, and the Wyrd and the Elpis portion of the Divine Fire as the Wyld.<br /> <br /> I remember when somebody was trying to make a composite cosmology from WoD and ChroD, I proposed the Triad (Wyld, Weaver, Wyrm) become the Quintad (Wyld makes raw stuff, Weaver makes refined stuff, Wyld arranges stuff into narratives, Wyrm breaks down the stuff that's no longer useful, and the Fire renders the trash into usable reagents for the Wyld to make raw stuff with). I wonder if, faced with the cosmology conflict, the various primeval forces might realign themselves that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:08:33-07:00","id":982834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=982276#post982276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey those Silver Ladder guys seem pretty reasonable, way better than our own Reality Deviants, we should enter a non-aggression pact and not try to fuck them over because a three-way war is a pretty retarded idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Use of the word &quot;retarded&quot; in this context is considered a slur. Don't use it this way; better yet, you should really avoid using it at all.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:28:27-07:00","id":982931,"title":"","content":"A person retards the advancement of society when using the word &quot;retard&quot; inappropriately. (It's actually a perfectly good word for &quot;to slow something down&quot;, so it's pretty annoying when people use it as an insult.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:04:31-07:00","id":982951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=982834#post982834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:red\">Use of the word &quot;retarded&quot; in this context is considered a slur. Don't use it this way; better yet, you should really avoid using it at all.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course, sorry.<br /> <br /> What it <i>really says </i>is that it's a very bad idea, and it has been written like that the whole time, because I would never make a mistake like that and you must have been blinded by the Lie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It won't happen again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:12:48-07:00","id":982955,"title":"","content":"To make up for my very dumb mistake, I'm now busy writing a Technocrat's Dossier on the creatures of the CofD.<br /> <br /> It's looking to be at least two-three pages long in it's base format and will currently involve a dossier on every Major Template as well as Spirits, Ghosts and Angels.<br /> <br /> Are there any other stuff people might want on it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:57:07-07:00","id":982970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=982955#post982955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To make up for my very dumb mistake, I'm now busy writing a Technocrat's Dossier on the creatures of the CofD.<br /> <br /> It's looking to be at least two-three pages long in it's base format and will currently involve a dossier on every Major Template as well as Spirits, Ghosts and Angels.<br /> <br /> Are there any other stuff people might want on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a request, but advice:<br /> <br /> You think you can make the NWO come off as condescending as possible when talking about changelings? <br /> <br /> It seems like they'd have person-shaped blind spots when thinking about the effects abuse has on people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:07:42-07:00","id":983017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=982970#post982970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not a request, but advice:<br /> <br /> You think you can make the NWO come off as condescending as possible when talking about changelings?<br /> <br /> It seems like they'd have person-shaped blind spots when thinking about the effects abuse has on people.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmm, on one hand I can totally see where you're coming from, but on the other hand the NWO are also literally the psychologists of the Conventions and I very much like them.<br /> <br /> I think I'll try and alternate between them, making it something like this:<br /> <br /> The so-called Changelings are men and women of the masses who have been abducted by a strange subspecies of EDE (See, Dossier: Fae), and xenografted with alien DNA. Their abilities are often strange and almost nonsensical, suggesting perhaps that they were not designed for the Earthen athmosphere. Likewise, Changelings often possess small degrees of psychic powers, usually manifesting as Propability Manipulation (See: Noetic Theory) or innate talents for hyperpsych or hyperstat. Changelings make excellent field assets due to their subtlety and the ease of convincing them of the ultimate good and necessity of the Union. Most Changelings have already been exposed to some degree of abuse, often traumatizing them, making many almost grateful for the lower levels of Conditioning. The nonstandard approach that a Changeling's xenografts gives them to situations does not lend itself to direct power or brutal strength, but instead makes them clever in their approaches.<br /> <br /> The most important aspects of Changeling metaphysiology is their ability to detect the use of Enlightened Science however, as well as their innate hyperpsych understanding, which allows them to force people into keeping their word. The first of these abilities, refers to a Changeling's ability to practice &quot;kenning&quot; as they refer to it, an innate sense that allows them to perceive both Enlightened Science as well as Reality Deviancy of almost any kind. As this ability is more pronounced with their mental stability, a strategy that involves offerings of trust, openness and friendship is suggested in order to win them over. The second ability refers to a Changeling's ability to bind people to their agreements on the <i>exact words</i>. This ability is of utmost importance, and therefore it is important that one does not stress the desire to have those that show exceptional skill in it join the Union, but instead slowly win them over to our cause in order to not risk losing them.<br /> <br /> Due to their abuse, most Changelings are willing to side with us, once we hint that we may help them with their issues in fitting into society again, this makes them excellent targets for recruitment attempts by us, and in reverse makes them harder for Reality Deviants to recruit since they cannot provide the same promises of social security and stability that we can provide. Thus, the fifth Precept of Damian, and the third Mission Protocol are both revoked when dealing with Changelings as it might still be possible to realign them with our current scientific knowledge.<br /> <br /> In general, a careful &quot;carrots&quot; strategy of approach is recommended with Changelings.<br /> <br /> As enemies of the Union they are incredibly open to psychological warfare and conventional attack methods. Changelings almost universally have a xenografted Dimensional Mat-Trans Emulator that allows them to escape from most forms of confinement with ease, meaning that the most effective ways of containing one would be sedatives and draining of their reserves as well as a constant tending to by Bobs, Lauras or other similar Constructs with low-functioning or muted emotional packages. All of this would have to be reinforced by a constant influx of hyperpsych aimed at reinforcing their trust in lawful authority.<br /> <br /> Proper strikes against an actual Changeling &quot;Freehold&quot; is best performed with a combination of psychological warfare and conventional attacks. An Operative strike team should sow paranoia and take out key leaders to contain with the method described above, while Iterators and Void Engineers would respectively deal with anyone attempting to escape by mundane means and paranormal means. Luckily for us, Changeling xenografts seem to afflict them with an allergy to ferrous compounds, making them incredibly easy targets for even a standard Union-issue railgun, with no need for heavier ordnance such as ERASR rifles or MAULR gear.<br /> -Operative Jane Bautista<br /> <br /> It's not exactly condescending, but it does go &quot;hey look, Changelings have huge psychological weaknesses, let's exploit them to get them on our side.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:11:18-07:00","id":983019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=983017#post983017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hmmm, on one hand I can totally see where you're coming from, but on the other hand the NWO are also literally the psychologists of the Conventions and I very much like them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I get that, it's just that the NWO strike me as the kind of people who see the statistics and instantly assume they know everything about that person just by knowing &quot;they were abused&quot;.<br /> <br /> Your writeup shows that, so good work!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:25:05-07:00","id":983022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=983019#post983019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I get that, it's just that the NWO strike me as the kind of people who see the statistics and instantly assume they know everything about that person just by knowing &quot;they were abused&quot;.<br /> <br /> Your writeup shows that, so good work!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the way I like to write the NWO (or rather the Ivory Tower) is to go full-on &quot;well-meaning but elitist academic talks about the real world&quot;, which usually ends up pretty accurately.<br /> <br /> Whereas if this was written by an Operative it would go &quot;this is a Changeling. It can do this. Therefore you need to have one in your Amalgam RIGHT FUCKING NOW. Otherwise, this is how you deal with them as enemies.&quot;<br /> <br /> Much more simplistic, but less condescending because the Operatives are actually able to remember that grey as something between white and black exists.<br /> <br /> And thanks for the complement! ^_^ <br /> <br /> I love writing for the Technocracy, so it's really a pleasure to do this sort of thing. Vampires and Beasts will be written by a Progenitor, werewolves and hunters by a Syndic, mages and sin-eaters by a Void Engineer, prometheans and mummies by an Iterator and finally changelings and demons by an NWO-Technocrat (why is there nothing to call a member of the NWO?).<br /> <br /> I'm especially excited for writing about hunters-as-social-phenomenon from the viewpoint of a Syndic for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:26:06-07:00","id":983116,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?392895-necro-n-oWoD-In-character-Crossover-Discussions&amp;highlight=nwod+owod+crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Here </a>is the RPG.net thread where they did this. I like the technocrat quotes for CofD werewolves in it, but they were written for 1st ed cofd.<br /> <br /> Also, Garou get mad jealous of Uratha being able to have &quot;normal&quot; children with each other, while BSDs and Bale hounds compare notes until they get into a game of &quot;if you're so evil than eat this baby/ More evil than thou art&quot; that results in the destruction of Charleston..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:16:15-07:00","id":983357,"title":"","content":"The Bale Hounds and Black Spiral Dancers seem to have an in-build difference. The Dancers working internally, especially with the Black Labyrinth, focusing on corrupting themselves, and the Bale Hounds externally, corrupting others.<br /> <br /> They would get along well until their end goals came up, Bale Hounds don't want the end of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:23:37-07:00","id":983362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=983357#post983357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would get along well until their end goals came up, Bale Hounds don't want the end of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not - all their stuff is there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:28:12-07:00","id":983564,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the Umbra would be in for an unpleasant shock if it and the Shadow fused. With how savage and predatory Shadow spirits are things could get very messy very quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:07:40-07:00","id":983711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=983564#post983564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that the Umbra would be in for an unpleasant shock if it and the Shadow fused. With how savage and predatory Shadow spirits are things could get very messy very quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Invasive Species, spirit-style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:08:33-07:00","id":983712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=981750#post981750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I'll be killed and reanimated. I didn't know that. Kind of funny that there wasn't any interest then, considering how staunch Promethean fans are now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, it was only a page or so, and I think the WoD ended soon after, so it was easy for many to miss. I don't recall if they were explicitely said to be created by Magi or not...<br /> <br /> Incidentally, what started this thread was a debate I had with a friend about the two Demon games and the Translation Guides. Those games are SOOO different, that I honestly don't see a point to translating your characters; you're really better off just creating a Descent PC from scratch, and just giving it the same name as your Fallen PC!<br /> <br /> This led me to make the observation that, if a Requiem Vampire met a Masquerade Vampire, then they would recognize each other as vamps despite their differences, and the same for Werewolves, Mages, Mummies, etc. Demons, otoh, are the main ones that would walk right past each other, IF they could even sense each other in the first place, seeing absolutely *nothing* in common with each other. <br /> <br /> I still feel this way, but I must admit, there are a couple of interesting ideas for interaction between the two in this thread that hadn't occurred to me! So thanks for that...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 10-07-2016, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:18:46-07:00","id":983717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=983116#post983116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Garou get mad jealous of Uratha being able to have &quot;normal&quot; children with each other, while BSDs and Bale hounds compare notes until they get into a game of &quot;if you're so evil than eat this baby/ More evil than thou art&quot; that results in the destruction of Charleston..</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but what happens when, inevitably, Uratha breeds with Garou?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At least the Pure's job gets MUCH harder, as they suddenly have to deal with *many more* Moon-Blessed!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:51:57-07:00","id":983737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=983712#post983712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This led me to make the observation that, if a Requiem Vampire met a Masquerade Vampire, then they would recognize each other as vamps despite their differences, and the same for Werewolves, Mages, Mummies, etc. Demons, otoh, are the main ones that would walk right past each other, IF they could even sense each other in the first place, seeing absolutely *nothing* in common with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>oChangelings and nChangelings wouldn't be terribly fond of each other, either. Really, I think oChangelings would probably be on better terms with Beasts, really. Personified terror isn't terribly fun, but there's not much banality to be found in a giant, eight-winged cat dragon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=983717#post983717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, but what happens when, inevitably, Uratha breeds with Garou?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Still technically Werewolf + Werewolf. Can you say... Perfect Metis?<br /> <hr />So, can we get fangames in on this? Because the Radiant Court Princesses are pretty much everything the oChangelings could ask for, and there's a lot of parallels (reincarnated beings from magical kingdoms who fight to hold back the Darkness/Banality), and Genii have the weird situation of functioning much like Ascension Magi, but with the odd situation of being objectively wrong.<br /> <br /> And I just wanna know what they all think of Leviathans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T22:54:59-07:00","id":983769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=983737#post983737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> oChangelings and nChangelings wouldn't be terribly fond of each other, either. Really, I think oChangelings would probably be on better terms with Beasts, really. Personified terror isn't terribly fun, but there's not much banality to be found in a giant, eight-winged cat dragon.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>BUT Trolls and Sidhe would still recognize Ogres and Fairest as fae, was my point. Or would they? The exteriors might match, but the latter wouldn't have the nature of the Dreaming about them...but Beasts certainly would, you're right about that! <br /> <br /> Don't know a lot about the fan-splats, tbh. What <i>are</i> Radiant Court Princesses, Genii and Leviathans, exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T05:37:14-07:00","id":983864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=983769#post983769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BUT Trolls and Sidhe would still recognize Ogres and Fairest as fae, was my point. Or would they? The exteriors might match, but the latter wouldn't have the nature of the Dreaming about them...but Beasts certainly would, you're right about that!<br /> <br /> Don't know a lot about the fan-splats, tbh. What <i>are</i> Radiant Court Princesses, Genii and Leviathans, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Princesses (at least of the Radiant Courts): Magical Girls (and Guys) fighting Fear and the manifestations of the corruptive Darkness. As well as normal human inhumanity.<br /> <br /> Genius: Mad Scientists who can created Wonders based on off and incorrect theories (think space craft or ray guns as if Lumeniferous Aether were actually real).<br /> <br /> Leviathan: The heirs (and incarnations?) of ancient sea monsters, part human, part beast, part god. Can grow from human to incredible size, and have a mind breaking (and cultist making) aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T07:44:43-07:00","id":983917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=983769#post983769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BUT Trolls and Sidhe would still recognize Ogres and Fairest as fae, was my point. Or would they? The exteriors might match, but the latter wouldn't have the nature of the Dreaming about them...but Beasts certainly would, you're right about that!<br /> <br /> Don't know a lot about the fan-splats, tbh. What <i>are</i> Radiant Court Princesses, Genii and Leviathans, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>The Radiant Princesses are the &quot;good&quot; faction of <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/home\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Noble</a>, in which you play Magical Girls (well, not necessarily girls, but that was the main inspiration) fighting a losing battle against Darkness.</li> <li><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/moochava/genius\" target=\"_blank\">Geniuses: the Transgression</a> is the &quot;mad scientist&quot; fansplat, although their Wonders run on magic-powered pseudoscience, and was really strongly influenced by Mage: the Asenscion.</li> <li><a href=\"https://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/LeviathanTempest:Main_Page\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a> is centered around the Leviathans, people who find out that they're basically members of kaiju/Cthulhu hybrid race that has been in continuous collapse since the Stone Age, and they're surrounded by a psychic field that slowly turns people into cultists just by being around them.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T09:40:25-07:00","id":984469,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I'd seen a couple of refs to those around. I'd wondered how Genius was really different from the Sons of Ether...that might be an interesting meet up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T19:28:11-07:00","id":984717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=982955#post982955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To make up for my very dumb mistake, I'm now busy writing a Technocrat's Dossier on the creatures of the CofD.<br /> <br /> It's looking to be at least two-three pages long in it's base format and will currently involve a dossier on every Major Template as well as Spirits, Ghosts and Angels.<br /> <br /> Are there any other stuff people might want on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to hear the Technocrats thoughts on Sin-Eaters, and how they are a disorganized but tight knit group.<br /> <br /> maybe also point out the sin-eaters craziness for willingly pissoff the Death Gods called Kerberoi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T21:13:03-07:00","id":984743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=984717#post984717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd love to hear the Technocrats thoughts on Sin-Eaters, and how they are a disorganized but tight knit group.<br /> <br /> maybe also point out the sin-eaters craziness for willingly pissoff the Death Gods called Kerberoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think it's possible that they could be mistaken, at first glance, for Death-centered Ascension Mages with really weird Avatars, especially given how much of their magic runs on personal mythologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T01:07:49-07:00","id":984779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=984717#post984717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd love to hear the Technocrats thoughts on Sin-Eaters, and how they are a disorganized but tight knit group.<br /> <br /> maybe also point out the sin-eaters craziness for willingly pissoff the Death Gods called Kerberoi.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sin-Eaters and the Union's opinion on them are...<br /> <br /> <i>strange</i>.<br /> <br /> A Sin-Eater is a completely immortal, ridiculously powerful and almost freeform human-ghost fusion.<br /> <br /> This is a fucking nightmare waiting to happen, and thus the Union will be extremely fucking damn cautious around them. Yes, you can always get someone with Dimensional Science 3 to kill them, but it's <i>actually hurting them</i> that's the problem.<br /> <br /> Luckily for the Union, Sin-Eaters are a fractious and disorganized lot split into hundreds of different mythologies and ideas, otherwise they are a potential GODLIKE-class threat, like the Ravnos Antediluvian. They are kept as far away from Union infrastructure as possible and instead of bothering with even fighting them and wasting a lot of good men and women in the process, the Union will much rather just go &quot;take some money and cool stuff, now go the fuck away and don't bother us please&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Union will probably not even bother trying to ally with them except for those rare ones that get mythologies like &quot;ghosts don't actually exist and are just like, psychic imprints or fucking nanotech or whatever.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for Kerberoi...<br /> <br /> Well, those are probably a <i>huuuuuge fucking pain in the ass</i> for the Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T06:15:24-07:00","id":984842,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, Beast would be a Technocrat's nightmare (pun slightly intended). They have free access to all parts of the cosmos, they have a personal bas of operations with no clear physical location, and they have a natural talent for allying with and befriending other supernaturals. Not to mention their intrinsic powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T07:12:38-07:00","id":984866,"title":"","content":"Beast's general Opinion if the worlds did merge? &quot;WHOOOHOOOOOO!!!! More Family!&quot; &quot;Waitaminute ow lord these guys are worse then our ones to be around... LIGHTEN UP!&quot;<br /> In general the oWoD was alot more oppressive and less &quot;Hopeful&quot; the World was doomed and you Couldn't do anything to stop it. CofD you can change the world. Or atleast the part of it that you are in.. the World is not Doomed.<br /> <br /> Requim Vampires would be an interesting Counter to the Antediluvians since.. they have no blood ties to them and would be largely immune to most of the things that effect there Blood... (What with the Blood of Requim Vamps being ALIVE! and wanting to do things in its way...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T07:56:07-07:00","id":984877,"title":"","content":"The G-M literally has any CofD version of Gehenna locked in a vault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T08:09:24-07:00","id":984881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=984877#post984877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The G-M literally has any CofD version of Gehenna locked in a vault.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably all 13 flavours and Caine aswell.<br /> <br /> If it was a sudden &quot;Smash&quot; and everything just turned up the G-M would be working in the open for abit to get shit locked away and trying to seal up the world's endings. It would look at outworking the Weaver (Being an Industrial monolith would let it craft infrastructure faster), containing the Wyrm and sealing the Wyld. Asfar as i can tell anyway.<br /> <br /> It would send Agents out to secure the various Sleeping Vampies. Locking them away and making them tame/safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T14:42:24-07:00","id":986395,"title":"","content":"Too interesting a proposition, so little time. I'll let myself post without reading 4 pages first.<br /> <br /> VAMPIRES: For Requiem Kindred, the distinction is simple. They are quite used to numerous origins to their kind, and even to the eventual &quot;first vampire&quot; showing up. Their society is based more on the fact that by sheer coincidence their curses work in very similar ways. So, no big deal. Partially.<br /> <br /> There is one thing Requiem Ones would find surprising, and maybe of concern. The way Cainites have an incredibly stable Blood Potency, to the point of it being partially hereditary. It is so stable, in fact, that those vampires call it Generation, and have a hard way to deal with their own rare deviations on the rule (like Diablerie). They would need some time to get used to it, but not a big deal, since they are already used to always begin unlife in the &quot;shallowest&quot; blood, and knowing that one day they will grow in power, Diablerie or not.<br /> <br /> Masquerade Cainites would have a harder time. First, for most the &quot;newcomers&quot; would defy all they know about the Curse, doesn't matter what legend about Kindred origin they believe. For most, though, it wouldn't make a great difference by itself. Blood Potence, though, would be a far greater concern for individual Cainies. It means that Generation isn't nearly as relevant to the Requiem Ones, that they don't have Weak Blooded in the same way, and that their elders can be even more fearsome, because they can <u><b>achieve</b></u> lower &quot;generations&quot;just with time. That's frightening from a Masquerade perspective.<br /> <br /> Since we're not discussing rules, I don't see the point on comparing other characteristics of the two. Distinctions on senses, and specially on Disciplines, can be simply waived for now as distinctions on rules, not setting.<br /> <br /> WEREWOLVES: Here the first connudrum comes with the very notion of contact, because both would be very attentive of such &quot;world collision&quot;. Once we get through this, there is still all sorts of problems. The Garou have the Pack as their social basis, that is true, but also the Caern and Sept, two institutions the Uratha lack altogether, and that would be the first point of strangeness. The Garou would find the Uratha unorganized, innefective and more of a strange kind of spirit than kin, like just another kind of Fera. The Uratha would find the Garou obsessive with control and with war.<br /> <br /> They would probably be able to make alliances or enter conflict in a case-by-case basis, and none would ever trust the other entirely, because of the disregard of one by the rules of the other. Uratha don't see the world directly in terms of Wyrm, and hardly cares about things outside pack territory. Garou not only don't care about interactions between worlds, except in terms of their own war, they actualy want to see the world whole again, and that means lowering the Gauntlet as much as they can.<br /> <br /> MAGES: Metaphisicaly speaking, the two groups have nothing to do with one another. Awakening's true magic comes from a reality more &quot;real&quot; than the known world, from old misteries, from a link with something outside the character that makes him aware of truths above the world we perceive. Ascension's true magic is about shaping reality to one's own belief, about the power of the collective human mind and the power of challenging this common perception, about dedicating oneself to something until you can take things in your own hands and make it true, doesn't matter how much other people disbelieve, there is an Avatar, a piece of divinity, but instead of linking the mage to something bigger, it makes the mage herself bigger.<br /> <br /> But both groups are also used to learn by themselves and live (to some degree) with people they disagree. The Nine Traditions would welcome the Pentacle and the Free Council with the same caution they have with one another, already, and the Pentacle would do the same to them. There would be some discussion about how to mingle the groups until they become aware of how different they are, and then they simply stay allied but distinct structures. Marauders, Nefandi, Scellesti and the like would probably remain distinct groups, trying to manipulate or hide as they always did.<br /> <br /> The greater shock would be between Seers and Technocracy. Both have good numbers and the &quot;domain of the status quo&quot;. But are, at the same time, astoundingly far from each other. They would hunt one another inside the power structures of society, and probably reach for their more traditional enemies for an alliance. The bid of the Seers for power and control of magic is common among Ascension's Mages, but at least Tech and Trad as groups always cared something about the world at large. Those &quot;Seers&quot; are just plainly power-hungry, and maybe the Tech can get some help to deal with them. Technocracy, on the other hand, want to wipe &quot;dangerous beliefs&quot; from this world, while the Seers never cared too much about such abstract concepts. That conflict would be the focus of the next hard decisions of both Traditions and Pentacle/FC, to whom ally, if to someone at all.<br /> <br /> CHANGELINGS: Probably Dreaming's fae would scare the hell out of the Lost at first. Those things <u>are</u> True Fae by themselves. The Fae would, by their part, wonder the immunity of the Lost to Banality. In the end of the day, they would probably live apart with some careful contact, but this contact would be as passionate as one could expect, since both are, still, moved by emotions, stories and relationships swored as an Oath.<br /> <br /> DEMONS: Even more than any of the previous, the Fallen of both groups have absolutely nothing to do with one another. There is, surely, clear similarities between their stories, but that's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T14:54:03-07:00","id":986406,"title":"","content":"The Lodge of Garm the God-Killer would love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T04:35:17-07:00","id":986677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=986395#post986395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The greater shock would be between Seers and Technocracy. Both have good numbers and the &quot;domain of the status quo&quot;. But are, at the same time, astoundingly far from each other. They would hunt one another inside the power structures of society, and probably reach for their more traditional enemies for an alliance. The bid of the Seers for power and control of magic is common among Ascension's Mages, but at least Tech and Trad as groups always cared something about the world at large. Those &quot;Seers&quot; are just plainly power-hungry, and maybe the Tech can get some help to deal with them. Technocracy, on the other hand, want to wipe &quot;dangerous beliefs&quot; from this world, while the Seers never cared too much about such abstract concepts. That conflict would be the focus of the next hard decisions of both Traditions and Pentacle/FC, to whom ally, if to someone at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I mentioned earlier that the Silver Ladder's ideals are surprisingly close to those of the Technocracy, except described through mysticism instead of scientific terms.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Guardians and the Arrow would also find a lot of sympathizers amongst the Union.<br /> <br /> The Mysterium less so, while the Free Council would be a target of scorn and the Seers, even worse than the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile:<br /> <br /> Amusingly, the God-Machine and the Technocracy will absolutely abhor one another.<br /> <br /> Because the Technocracy is all about the continued protection (and &quot;guidance&quot;) of humanity against supernatural oppressors (and helpers), while the God-Machine is all about the status quo and manipulating humanity for it's own ends.<br /> <br /> Sadly, the Revised-era Technocracy isn't really in a position to do much against it, their primary attack force is preoccupied with Threat Null, and won't have the resources to go into a war with something on the scale of the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> Now, the 2e-era Technocracy however...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T05:47:58-07:00","id":986703,"title":"","content":"Even with all the similarities, the Technocracy won't allow at first for the mystic view of the Pentacle. They will have a better time allying with the Traditions.<br /> <br /> But you're right, and there's a lot behind that. On the long run, though, it is impossible to tell what will happen. Given how things were at the dawn of Revised, I would say that the current Tech and Traditions war will ed in a truce and reformulation, as the Tech divides into two major groups, one of with don't care with mysticism if humanity is cared for, and a similar schism happens to the Traditions, with a great faction thinking that humanity's well-being <u>is</u> too great a price for personal Ascension. This could result in a mixed group more alligned with the Pentacle proper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T10:59:42-07:00","id":986850,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to imagine what sort of philosophical implosion would happen to the Garou when they meet the Uratha and realize there's a world just as screwed up as theirs without anything like the Wyrm to blame it on. <br /> <br /> I don't see Vigil hunters having much difficulty accepting the Imbued. They've basically just got an elaborate Endowment. The real question is whether Vigil hunters with Endowments would appear as supernatural to Imbued &quot;Hunter Sight.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:16:36-07:00","id":986884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=986850#post986850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to imagine what sort of philosophical implosion would happen to the Garou when they meet the Uratha and realize there's a world just as screwed up as theirs without anything like the Wyrm to blame it on.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, everyone's pretty sure the blame lies on the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> That's probably what always makes me associate the Apocalypse tribes with the Pure. I could see the tribes placing the blame on the Forsaken and, if things could be fixed as the Pure say, giving a big screw you to humanity and working at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-13-2016, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:22:36-07:00","id":986887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=986850#post986850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to imagine what sort of philosophical implosion would happen to the Garou when they meet the Uratha and realize there's a world just as screwed up as theirs without anything like the Wyrm to blame it on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonsense. All evil is the Wyrm, these so-called &quot;Uratha&quot; are obviously attempting to mislead us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see Vigil hunters having much difficulty accepting the Imbued. They've basically just got an elaborate Endowment. The real question is whether Vigil hunters with Endowments would appear as supernatural to Imbued &quot;Hunter Sight.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I can tell you they won't like the Lucifuge. Though, Fallen Demons would probably have the Lucifuge's back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T02:18:01-07:00","id":987159,"title":"","content":"1: Cainite Heresy and the Imbued meet.<br /> <br /> 2: Talk about Messengers.<br /> <br /> 3: TheFuckIsThisShit.png<br /> <br /> 4: Greatest ponzi scheme in the history of two worlds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T03:17:35-07:00","id":987169,"title":"","content":"So this one was inspired by a conversation in the CWoD forum:<br /> <br /> The Masquerade version of protean's first power lets you see in the dark but makes your eyes glow. What this looks like isn't specified all that clearly. I propose that for this crossover it is near-identical to Strix possession, for maximum luls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T04:58:25-07:00","id":987196,"title":"","content":"Looking/thinking on it further i feel Beast would find the oWoD Fallen/Demons to be Kin... they may even accept Lucifer as some form of &quot;Dark Father&quot; as a memory of some ancient being that &quot;Fell&quot; for Humanity/Disagreed with the Plan etc. The resonance of that type of tale would be immense in the Dream.<br /> <br /> I Also think Geisters and the Kuei-Jin would get on quite well... they have both Seen Hell... they know they need to do better to stay out of it (Less so for the Geisters.. but Yeah)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:27:19-07:00","id":987445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987196#post987196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking/thinking on it further i feel Beast would find the oWoD Fallen/Demons to be Kin... they may even accept Lucifer as some form of &quot;Dark Father&quot; as a memory of some ancient being that &quot;Fell&quot; for Humanity/Disagreed with the Plan etc. The resonance of that type of tale would be immense in the Dream.<br /> <br /> I Also think Geisters and the Kuei-Jin would get on quite well... they have both Seen Hell... they know they need to do better to stay out of it (Less so for the Geisters.. but Yeah)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah, I forgot!<br /> <br /> I think Kuei-Jin and Lost would get on like a house on fire. Tokyo is outright crawling with changelings, and they have a nearly identical set of events in their life-the difference is that the Yama Kings are honest about what they are.<br /> <br /> I think Devil-Tigers would love a chance to help the Lost turn the Huntsmen's mind games upon themselves. In return, I expect the Courts might try to figure out a way to tame <i>chih-mei </i>by invading their dreams, forcefully clamping down on the P'o long enough to listen to the Dharmas and making recruitment a lot easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-14-2016, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T18:04:24-07:00","id":987519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=986887#post986887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nonsense. All evil is the Wyrm, these so-called &quot;Uratha&quot; are obviously attempting to mislead us.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>But what happens when they use their &quot;sense Wyrm&quot; power on them? Or on anything clearly &quot;twisted and evil&quot; from NWoD that isn't actually OF the Wyrm? <br /> <br /> BTW, I think I've read that 2e Forsaken has given the Uratha quite the power-boost...are they a match for Garou now? And do they now have anything like Caerns and Septs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:54:28-07:00","id":987562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987519#post987519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what happens when they use their &quot;sense Wyrm&quot; power on them? Or on anything clearly &quot;twisted and evil&quot; from NWoD that isn't actually OF the Wyrm?<br /> <br /> BTW, I think I've read that 2e Forsaken has given the Uratha quite the power-boost...are they a match for Garou now? And do they now have anything like Caerns and Septs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think the Uratha have a lot more spiritual powers than the Garou (could be wrong, it's been ages since I read Apocalypse properly), so if they leverage their territory's Shadow ecology, I think the Forsaken could win on their own turf without too much difficulty, and they'd be decently dangerous if they work smartly. It helps that the WoD Werewolves strike me as being kind of arrogant.<br /> <br /> Near as I can tell, &quot;Caerns&quot; are relatively analogous to Loci, and Septs aren't really a distinct thing in Forsaken culture, although most Packs who live near a Locus will protect them like a Sept would protect a Caern.<br /> <br /> Though, I had a thought. Would it be a Breaking Point for a Forsaken to kill a Garou? Because they are werewolves, but I don't know if they count as &quot;The People&quot; in Uratha terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T03:00:26-07:00","id":987687,"title":"","content":"That's an interesting question, though I think, given how Breaking Points work, that it would depend on the particular view of the killer. But on an emotional, subconscious, level. Probably both groups would have a hard time, anyway, deciding if the other counts for its own law on not killing werewolves.<br /> <br /> I still don't think that the similarity between Loci and Caerns should be a thing IC. Even if they have the same mechanical function, to Uratha a Locus is just a (very) valuable tool. It is rare, it is potent, it needs care, but it isn't sacred as a rule. For Uratha, it is perfectly valid to destroy a Locus that serves an enemy or just isn't useful. To Garou, a Caern is the most sacred of places, and never should be lightly treated, much less destroyed or desecrated.<br /> <br /> Also, the Locus is still simpler and more common than a Caern, it is just an emotionally charged object and the area around. In comparison, it is just like a somewhat more powerful fetish. And even those aren't sacred to Uratha as they are to Garou. I don't think the Garou would see with good eyes the relative callousness of the Uratha over fetishes and sacred places, nor would the Uratha like the extremist approach of the Garou over everything in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T09:13:09-07:00","id":987782,"title":"","content":"Demons and Traditionalist Mages are gonna love each other.<br /> <br /> The Union is not going to want the Seers to remain in power, but they probably won't declare war on them due to the difficulties in fighting an entrenched foe like the Seers. Instead they'll work through proxies and conceal their traces through Enlightened Science, NWO will play spy games with Panopticon and the Syndicate will match Mammon pound for pound in economic warfare.<br /> <br /> I don't know who would win, but I know that it won't look pretty, and to anyone who has been used to either side's power, it will be a horrifying sight to see two conspiracies, so powerful that they control their respective realities battle. A conflict of this scope and size will <i>define</i> other supernatural societies with it's magnitude.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the Union will win, but it can go either way honestly. Though the Union has them handily beat at the spy games part, the Seers have Panopticon as their primary force in these kinds of operations, while the Union has the Operatives, the Enforcers, the Watchers and the Feed.<br /> <br /> On the brute force angle, the Union has ATLAS Units, who will quickly become nightmare fuel in the nWoD. For those who don't know what an ATLAS is, it's basically a mage that has been so broken by NWO torture and brainwashed by Processing that his personality has been reworked completely, the only thing left of him, is basically his brain, everything else is a Primium (read: What Thaumium wishes to be when it grows up) skeleton, plated in even more Primium and equipped with all sorts of nasty weapons, like spike throwers that literally throw people meters and impale them on walls. They can also do magic like a mage while being almost immune to any sort of magic or supernatural abilities, and tanky enough to make an actual tank jealous.<br /> <br /> To be fair to nWoD, they are also nightmare fuel in cWoD, so they won't be alone in considering them scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T09:39:39-07:00","id":987798,"title":"","content":"What I wanna know, though is whether OMage has an equivalent to NMage's Archmages? Because the Archmages are some pretty scary, high-level stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T10:18:39-07:00","id":987810,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it has archmages. I'm not sure if they're as powerful as awakening archmages, but they do exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:13:08-07:00","id":987844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987687#post987687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't think that the similarity between Loci and Caerns should be a thing IC. Even if they have the same mechanical function, to Uratha a Locus is just a (very) valuable tool. It is rare, it is potent, it needs care, but it isn't sacred as a rule. For Uratha, it is perfectly valid to destroy a Locus that serves an enemy or just isn't useful. To Garou, a Caern is the most sacred of places, and never should be lightly treated, much less destroyed or desecrated.<br /> <br /> Also, the Locus is still simpler and more common than a Caern, it is just an emotionally charged object and the area around. In comparison, it is just like a somewhat more powerful fetish. And even those aren't sacred to Uratha as they are to Garou. I don't think the Garou would see with good eyes the relative callousness of the Uratha over fetishes and sacred places, nor would the Uratha like the extremist approach of the Garou over everything in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly accurate. Loci are thin spaces between the worlds, and the only places werewolves can reliably switch over without help. They're also incredibly valuable as fuel supplies, because Essence is hard to get without them. Defiling one is a Breaking Point, werewolves wouldn't dismiss them like that and they certainly aren't like fetishes, especially considering how they effect the world around them. They can be built, but it's not an easy thing to do, we had to do one in our story and it was pretty brutal but had drastic long-lasting experiences. I don't know if Garou can make Caerns.<br /> <br /> Regarding fetishes, even Apocalypse has 1-dot fetishes with minor benefits, and the ability to make new ones. It's mostly their klaives that have special significance because they're warriors. But the Uratha don't take fetishes lightly, p146, 'They guard fetishes more jealously due to their relative permanence and accrued history, and a gift of such an item is a matter of deep symbolism, emotion, and honor.'<br /> <br /> The idea that a perceived 'callousness' of the Uratha would make the Garou dislike them makes me think the Garou would become aligned with the Pure even more. The Fire-Touched view the Hisil as holy, no matter the damage it and its denizens can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-15-2016, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:37:38-07:00","id":987858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987844#post987844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Loci are thin spaces between the worlds, and the only places werewolves can reliably switch over without help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually as of The Pack they can also do so at their pack's Den.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:46:50-07:00","id":987863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987858#post987858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually as of The Pack they can also do so at their pack's Den.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which isn't reliable to werewolves since it only works for that pack, and requires help in the form of a Merit. They can also have a totem or fetish that causes Gauntlet Breach and any other number of special circumstances. A locus just requires a werewolf to get near one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:54:10-07:00","id":987868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987810#post987810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it has archmages. I'm not sure if they're as powerful as awakening archmages, but they do exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces 8 Archmasters can move <i>planets</i>.<br /> <br /> With Mind 9, you have become the mind of the entire universe at once.<br /> <br /> Most of them died in the Dimensional Anomaly though. The Progenitors <i>might</i> have a few of them left, and ex-Void Engineer Catherine Nichols possesses Dimensional Science 6.<br /> <br /> But as a general rule, they are even more ridiculously rare in cWoD than they are in nWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:08:20-07:00","id":987873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987863#post987863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which isn't reliable to werewolves since it only works for that pack, and requires help in the form of a Merit. They can also have a totem or fetish that causes Gauntlet Breach and any other number of special circumstances. A locus just requires a werewolf to get near one.</div> </div> </div> </div>We seem to be using different definitions of &quot;reliable&quot;. If your pack has a den, it's plenty reliable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:33:04-07:00","id":987892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987844#post987844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly accurate. Loci are thin spaces between the worlds, and the only places werewolves can reliably switch over without help. They're also incredibly valuable as fuel supplies, because Essence is hard to get without them. Defiling one is a Breaking Point, werewolves wouldn't dismiss them like that and they certainly aren't like fetishes, especially considering how they effect the world around them. They can be built, but it's not an easy thing to do, we had to do one in our story and it was pretty brutal but had drastic long-lasting experiences. I don't know if Garou can make Caerns.<br /> <br /> Regarding fetishes, even Apocalypse has 1-dot fetishes with minor benefits, and the ability to make new ones. It's mostly their klaives that have special significance because they're warriors. But the Uratha don't take fetishes lightly, p146, 'They guard fetishes more jealously due to their relative permanence and accrued history, and a gift of such an item is a matter of deep symbolism, emotion, and honor.'<br /> <br /> The idea that a perceived 'callousness' of the Uratha would make the Garou dislike them makes me think the Garou would become aligned with the Pure even more. The Fire-Touched view the Hisil as holy, no matter the damage it and its denizens can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Garou can make Caerns, but this is hugely costly, slow and dangerous, even if compared to a Locus. A single pack won't be ever able to make a Caern just by themselves, unless they're really powerful or in incredibly safe circumstances, and even them probably a weak one. Finding and reopening a closed Caern is already a daunting task, and is far easier (and comparable to making a Locus).<br /> <br /> I do know that Loci are all of that, but really, Caerns are <u><b>sacred</b></u> to Garou. Defiling one isn't just a &quot;Breaking Point&quot;, it is considered one of the most heinous crimes, commonly dealt with death sentence.<br /> <br /> As for fetishes, it goes on similarly. Yes, Klaives and Gran-Klaives are among their more sacred ones. But even minor fetishes are considered with religious relevance, if far less than a Caern. An Uratha will be jealous of her fetishe, but to Garou it is like a saint's image to a catholic in the XII century. It is actualy a <u>crime</u> to break one unless absolutely needed, and even then you're punished with lost renown for not finding another way.<br /> <br /> To finish, indeed. The Garou are very similar to the Pure, more than the Forsaken. It seems that the Pure are a kind of OoC mockery of the Garou Nation, its (not so) darkest side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:28:14-07:00","id":987938,"title":"","content":"Something struck me.<br /> <br /> Think of the hell most Traditions Mages have survived, <i>especially</i> when they're older and more experienced, and now compare to the Seers' more lax attitude with the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> Most Traditions Mages will probably look like war-veterans in the eyes of Pentacle Mages.<br /> <br /> Heh, we can have Golden Chalice commandoes providing military training to Pentacle Mages.<br /> <br /> After all, compared to the Pentacle, the Traditions have actual, trained commandoes that wage war against the hideously terrifying Technocratic Union that can field things such as &quot;mage with soak and health that would make a M1 Abrams tank blush&quot; pretty easily even in it's weakened state.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Seers are pretty powerful, but really not in the same ways as the Union. They tend to be unable to apply the same terrifying, direct force that the Union can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:46:14-07:00","id":987948,"title":"","content":"The Traditions seem to have more in common with the Unchained.<br /> <br /> While the aggression of the Seers is downplayed, they are incredibly powerful. Profane urims, Myrmidons and other Exarch-spawned sub-races, ochemata. They don't need to put the pressure on the Pentacle that the Technocracy do the Traditions because they've already won, and while mages can muck up things, there doesn't seem to be any real chance of the Exarchs being overthrown. To some Seers the Awakened might as well just be playtesters.<br /> <br /> Besides, the Arrow is all about military training and conflict-being-magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-15-2016, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T15:05:21-07:00","id":987951,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder what would happen when the two different kinds of Vampires begin to share blood. The different Clans appear to have become so similar to each other do to years of sharing blood between each other. This can be seen with the Jiang Shi in the Triangle. I suspect Generation might stop being a problem after a while. The descendants of Thin-Bloods with unique Disciplines might eventually become the origin of new Clans and Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Actually, seeing how persecuted Caitiffs usually are I could see them turning to CofD Kindred society for safety,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T15:10:59-07:00","id":987953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987948#post987948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Traditions seem to have more in common with the Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987948#post987948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the aggression of the Seers is downplayed, they are incredibly powerful. Profane urims, Myrmidons and other Exarch-spawned sub-races, ochemata. They don't need to put the pressure on the Pentacle that the Technocracy do the Traditions because they've already won, and while mages can muck up things, there doesn't seem to be any real chance of the Exarchs being overthrown. To some Seers the Awakened might as well just be playtesters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguing that the Union needs to put this pressure on the Traditions is incorrect. The Union <i>has won</i>.<br /> <br /> The Union keeps up the pressure on the Awakened because the Union never does anything by half, all Reality Deviance must be crushed and excised from the Consensus before reality is truly won.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987948#post987948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, the Arrow is all about military training and conflict-being-magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but every single Tradition has one, if not more militant societies.<br /> <br /> Every. Single. One.<br /> <br /> Like, the Golden Chalice are trained commandoes and spec ops, already from the get go, and then they get magic to toy around with.<br /> <br /> The Arrow remains a single Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T15:19:04-07:00","id":987955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987953#post987953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguing that the Union needs to put this pressure on the Traditions is incorrect. The Union <i>has won</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, they're still at a point they can be overthrown. It's sort of the whole point of the game, it's a war, not a slaughter. That was taken out in Awakening because, except for myths, the only real thing you can do is become an archmage and do what you care about. The Exarchs control reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, but every single Tradition has one, if not more militant societies.<br /> <br /> Every. Single. One.<br /> <br /> Like, the Golden Chalice are trained commandoes and spec ops, already from the get go, and then they get magic to toy around with.<br /> <br /> The Arrow remains a single Order. </div> </div> </div>This is another thing that differs between the games, the Orders aren't as disparate as the Traditions. They work together. It would be more accurate to consider the Diamond one big Tradition in comparison, their belief system involves the Supernal forming the basis of reality. Then the Free Council as a separate tradition, with their overarching belief being that reality, and especially humanity, forms the basis of the Supernal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T15:21:22-07:00","id":987956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987953#post987953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Arrow remains a single Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the Diamond Orders aren't four distinct factions that happen to get along, they're four wings of what is supposed to be the same organisation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T15:54:33-07:00","id":987975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987951#post987951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to wonder what would happen when the two different kinds of Vampires begin to share blood. The different Clans appear to have become so similar to each other do to years of sharing blood between each other. This can be seen with the Jiang Shi in the Triangle. I suspect Generation might stop being a problem after a while. The descendants of Thin-Bloods with unique Disciplines might eventually become the origin of new Clans and Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Actually, seeing how persecuted Caitiffs usually are I could see them turning to CofD Kindred society for safety,</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be kind of funny, seeing those haughty Cainite elders watch their lineages get reduced a singular Cainite Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T16:11:07-07:00","id":987984,"title":"","content":"Demon v Demon: Lucifer is the architect of the God-Machine. Why did Lucifer make the God-Machine? To drain the power from, and eventually destroy, the Earthbound. But they have grown wise to its ways and are now trying to turn the Angels against the God-Machine. But great Dagon, whose Reliquary is a machine in and of itself, has managed to integrate himself into the God-Machine, and is now taking over to destroy its rivals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T16:17:20-07:00","id":987987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987955#post987955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, they're still at a point they can be overthrown. It's sort of the whole point of the game, it's a war, not a slaughter. That was taken out in Awakening because, except for myths, the only real thing you can do is become an archmage and do what you care about. The Exarchs control reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if you play Revised no. The point of Revised is that it really isn't a war. It has never been.<br /> <br /> How would you go about overthrowing the Union? In every single edition, it was the point that this wasn't a war you could win, and that participating was foolish.<br /> <br /> In First Edition it was explicit that the Union had won, and that the Traditions simply tried to get by while striking back a few times.<br /> <br /> In Second Edition, the Union and the Technocracy were gathering their terrible power and accumulating their strength for a final calamitous battle, that the Union would probably win in the end.<br /> <br /> In Revised Edition, the most heroic and great thing you could do would be to run a soup kitchen instead of trying to restart the Ascension War and get even more Mages murdered.<br /> <br /> The Union's Inner Circle does not control reality, but that's because controlling reality is impossible in Ascension, the Inner Circle does however control the Masses' perception of reality, and he who controls the Masses controls the universe.<br /> <br /> Mage: The Ascension is a game where the human will is a thing of terrible power, and thus organizations that could harness that power held immense strength.<br /> <br /> I love the Seers, but I've yet to see something as horrible to fight against as an ATLAS.<br /> <br /> Well except for Ochemata, but those aren't exactly run-of-the-mill things that will fight you in coordinated squads supported by other Union combat assets.<br /> <br /> The war against the Union has never been a war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T16:18:40-07:00","id":987989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987984#post987984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon v Demon: Lucifer is the architect of the God-Machine. Why did Lucifer make the God-Machine? To drain the power from, and eventually destroy, the Earthbound. But they have grown wise to its ways and are now trying to turn the Angels against the God-Machine. But great Dagon, whose Reliquary is a machine in and of itself, has managed to integrate himself into the God-Machine, and is now taking over to destroy its rivals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, the God-Machine succeeded in its mission of scouring the world of God's Angels. <i>All of them</i>. Including Lucifer and the Fallen. Their combined essence was not <i>imprisoned</i> in the Inferno, but instead <i>became</i> the Inferno, their collective rage occasionally spilling out of Wounds and corrupting humans and Ephemeral beings. Any timeline in which the Inferno dissolves and frees the Fallen is locked away, like any other undesirable timeline, stored within the belly of the Inferno, making even free Demons still trapped within themselves without their knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T16:40:14-07:00","id":988001,"title":"","content":"It didn't occurred to me, but indeed. The sharing of blood could be the device behind so many disparate creatures becoming so alike. Specially if you consider that even a single clan in Requiem doesn't have to actualy be a single clan IC. That could make, with passing time, the Cainites turn more alike the Requiem's Kindred.<br /> <br /> But until then, they would have a tough time. Thin-Bloods and Caitiff would certainly look for protection among the Requiem. They are far less concerned with their blood weirdness, and can even consider it an asset. Their society simply have room for those vampires by default. It is a win-win situation for both sides, since the Cainites are bringing information on this new Kindred Clan. I don't think Cainite society will endure much in the long run as a distinct thing, with both Camarilla and Sabbat clueless about the Requiem Ones. Requiem Vampires simply have a far more stable (if insular) society, with more room for adaptation to this crisis, and even to incorporate all the Cainite without any significant change at all in their basic structure. Even the several distinct belief systems of the Cainite vampires (and diverse lineages, even the Laibon) would simply slip in as new Covenants, something the Requiem Society already saw numerous times.<br /> <br /> The same can't be said of other CoD splats. If a conflict ensues between Ascension and Awakening, I would bet on Ascension. It isn't a likely outcome at first (just Tech vs Seers), but if done, they're screwed on Awakening's side. Ascension Magi have, as noted, far more experience with war. They're kind of balanced in power, so this experience would make the difference. Even if Seers and Pentacle and FC ally against this threat, Traditions and Technocracy are as able to do so, as they already do in some circumstances. Both can create their war machines, but Ascension simply already have a lot of them done, a lot more in production, and the blueprints to keep this going on. The Arrow is about conflict, but mostly on a philosophical way. Ascension not only have a lot of warriors, every single one with more than two years as willworker is a guerrilla survivor.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is dangerously close to actual conflict being deflagrated between the &quot;lines&quot;, given the nature of the Garou Nation as a whole. And at first, the Nation would have far more power as an organized front. They actualy are one, something the Forsaken lack. To make things worse, the Pure wouldn't have much of a problem allying with the Nation (if not with unanimous consent), whyle the Forsaken can't say the same of the Wyrm (on most cases, at least). The advantage of the Forsaken, though, would came out with time. First, they are better at guerrilla as independent cells, since they work far better without any support above the Pack, whyle the Nation is a cracked monolith. Second, they can muster far easier the help of mortal institutions personaly, most of them being in good terms with the Wolf-Blooded. By the way, 2nd Edition Wolf-Blooded is an awesome asset, since they can convert any mortal supporter into a wolf-blooded with time and exposure. The Nation have to rely on Kinfolk, and I'm not sure if the Kinfolk will not try to change sides in this conflagration. Third, the Forsaken doesn't have any of the infinite number of prejudices of the Nation, so they're not against allying to anyone else in particular as a rule of thumb. They can approach in very ameanable ways to other Fera, less harmfull Weaver-Spirits, and even vampires and other creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T16:50:28-07:00","id":988007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987987#post987987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not if you play Revised no. The point of Revised is that it really isn't a war. It has never been.<br /> <br /> How would you go about overthrowing the Union? In every single edition, it was the point that this wasn't a war you could win, and that participating was foolish.<br /> <br /> In First Edition it was explicit that the Union had won, and that the Traditions simply tried to get by while striking back a few times.<br /> <br /> In Second Edition, the Union and the Technocracy were gathering their terrible power and accumulating their strength for a final calamitous battle, that the Union would probably win in the end.<br /> <br /> In Revised Edition, the most heroic and great thing you could do would be to run a soup kitchen instead of trying to restart the Ascension War and get even more Mages murdered.<br /> <br /> The Union's Inner Circle does not control reality, but that's because controlling reality is impossible in Ascension, the Inner Circle does however control the Masses' perception of reality, and he who controls the Masses controls the universe.<br /> <br /> Mage: The Ascension is a game where the human will is a thing of terrible power, and thus organizations that could harness that power held immense strength.<br /> <br /> I love the Seers, but I've yet to see something as horrible to fight against as an ATLAS.<br /> <br /> Well except for Ochemata, but those aren't exactly run-of-the-mill things that will fight you in coordinated squads supported by other Union combat assets.<br /> <br /> The war against the Union has never been a war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite true, jjust in the core, and there's a reason.<br /> <br /> First, that terrible battle alluded in 2nd Ed already happened in Revised. It was the Fall of Doissetep.<br /> <br /> But the entirety of the things that happened at the time (Magi war on Umbra, the Ghost Bomb, the Week of Nightmares, the appearance of the Red Star, the Rise and Death of Ravnos with yet another Bomb) just threw the universe out of balance completely. The Guide to Technocracy makes it clear that from that point on the Union had just an illusion of infinite power to keep things running. Actualy both groups were thorned, both still had a lot of power but not what they had earlier anymore, and neither controlled reallity, with the Universe stalling without anyone the wiser to why or how to stop it.<br /> <br /> On a side note, one of the scenarios presented in the book Time of Judgment: Ascension is a probable inspiration for Awakening, and maybe for the entire CoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T16:59:43-07:00","id":988011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988007#post988007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite true, jjust in the core, and there's a reason.<br /> <br /> First, that terrible battle alluded in 2nd Ed already happened in Revised. It was the Fall of Doissetep.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a valid interpretation of it, though not actually canon. The terrible battle could have been something even worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988007#post988007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the entirety of the things that happened at the time (Magi war on Umbra, the Ghost Bomb, the Week of Nightmares, the appearance of the Red Star, the Rise and Death of Ravnos with yet another Bomb) just threw the universe out of balance completely. The Guide to Technocracy makes it clear that from that point on the Union had just an illusion of infinite power to keep things running. Actualy both groups were thorned, both still had a lot of power but not what they had earlier anymore, and neither controlled reallity, with the Universe stalling without anyone the wiser to why or how to stop it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised Technocracy doesn't have it's ridiculous power, no. Though they can still field stuff like ATLAS units or Dracomorphs pretty casually. The Void Engineers have freaking spaceships and most Syndics can pretty casually run around with &quot;10L handgun&quot; or &quot;body armor that makes full plate look jealous&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Union has a huge amount of power to throw at problems, even after it's lessening.<br /> <br /> And it's still winning the War.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988007#post988007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a side note, one of the scenarios presented in the book Time of Judgment: Ascension is a probable inspiration for Awakening, and maybe for the entire CoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Highly likely, but it's ages since I read Ascension, and I really don't like that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T17:48:54-07:00","id":988021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988001#post988001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It didn't occurred to me, but indeed. The sharing of blood could be the device behind so many disparate creatures becoming so alike. Specially if you consider that even a single clan in Requiem doesn't have to actualy be a single clan IC. That could make, with passing time, the Cainites turn more alike the Requiem's Kindred.<br /> <br /> But until then, they would have a tough time. Thin-Bloods and Caitiff would certainly look for protection among the Requiem. They are far less concerned with their blood weirdness, and can even consider it an asset. Their society simply have room for those vampires by default. It is a win-win situation for both sides, since the Cainites are bringing information on this new Kindred Clan. I don't think Cainite society will endure much in the long run as a distinct thing, with both Camarilla and Sabbat clueless about the Requiem Ones. Requiem Vampires simply have a far more stable (if insular) society, with more room for adaptation to this crisis, and even to incorporate all the Cainite without any significant change at all in their basic structure. Even the several distinct belief systems of the Cainite vampires (and diverse lineages, even the Laibon) would simply slip in as new Covenants, something the Requiem Society already saw numerous times.<br /> <br /> The same can't be said of other CoD splats. If a conflict ensues between Ascension and Awakening, I would bet on Ascension. It isn't a likely outcome at first (just Tech vs Seers), but if done, they're screwed on Awakening's side. Ascension Magi have, as noted, far more experience with war. They're kind of balanced in power, so this experience would make the difference. Even if Seers and Pentacle and FC ally against this threat, Traditions and Technocracy are as able to do so, as they already do in some circumstances. Both can create their war machines, but Ascension simply already have a lot of them done, a lot more in production, and the blueprints to keep this going on. The Arrow is about conflict, but mostly on a philosophical way. Ascension not only have a lot of warriors, every single one with more than two years as willworker is a guerrilla survivor.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is dangerously close to actual conflict being deflagrated between the &quot;lines&quot;, given the nature of the Garou Nation as a whole. And at first, the Nation would have far more power as an organized front. They actualy are one, something the Forsaken lack. To make things worse, the Pure wouldn't have much of a problem allying with the Nation (if not with unanimous consent), whyle the Forsaken can't say the same of the Wyrm (on most cases, at least). The advantage of the Forsaken, though, would came out with time. First, they are better at guerrilla as independent cells, since they work far better without any support above the Pack, whyle the Nation is a cracked monolith. Second, they can muster far easier the help of mortal institutions personaly, most of them being in good terms with the Wolf-Blooded. By the way, 2nd Edition Wolf-Blooded is an awesome asset, since they can convert any mortal supporter into a wolf-blooded with time and exposure. The Nation have to rely on Kinfolk, and I'm not sure if the Kinfolk will not try to change sides in this conflagration. Third, the Forsaken doesn't have any of the infinite number of prejudices of the Nation, so they're not against allying to anyone else in particular as a rule of thumb. They can approach in very ameanable ways to other Fera, less harmfull Weaver-Spirits, and even vampires and other creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't dismiss the Awakened so easily. For one, the Traditions don't really have a reason to pick a fight with the Awakened. In fact, it seems likely they might form an alliance in an &quot;enemy of my enemy way.&quot; The Pentacle and the Seers do have common cause to work together though and the Seers have Ochemata backup. While the Technocracy might have an edge, the fight is far from one-sided.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T18:03:10-07:00","id":988026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988021#post988021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't dismiss the Awakened so easily. For one, the Traditions don't really have a reason to pick a fight with the Awakened. In fact, it seems likely they might form an alliance in an &quot;enemy of my enemy way.&quot; The Pentacle and the Seers do have common cause to work together though and the Seers have Ochemata backup. While the Technocracy might have an edge, the fight is far from one-sided.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The fight is definitely not one-sided, for one there is the fact that the Union might back the Pentacle over the Seers actually.<br /> <br /> And the Traditions have sided with the Union before, during World War II. It could in fact likely end in the hilarious situation where we have a Union-Traditions-Pentacle alliance against the Seers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T18:11:47-07:00","id":988030,"title":"","content":"As I said, it isn't a likely outcome. The most probable one is to the Tech prioritize the Seers as target as soon as they learn about the Seers. From that point on, it isn't easy to determine because there are other actors in play (like Traditions, Pentacle and Free Council, not to mention Scelesti and Nefandi), and those are all wildcards for such scenario. With all the context, the fight is far from one-sided, indeed. But at this post, I was talking about <u>the case</u> of Awakening vs Ascension war happening. Mage is certainly the most complex scenario in this regard.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6042_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6042\" data-vbnamecard=\"6042\">ManusDomine</a> <br /> 1- The terrible battle was <u>at least</u> that powerful, and Doissetep felled anyway;<br /> 2- As I said, yes, they still have a huge power. But believe, the Traditions also have. Both are a lot weakened, but still scary. Though it is impossible to say what side suffered most, it made things more balanced because it is easier to tip the balance now;<br /> 3- Guide to Technocracy directly states that the Union power is far from enough to keep things with such certainty anymore. It also states directly that the Consensus is getting out of control;<br /> 4- Just for the record, both are still on par with the Awakening and far more used and prepared for war. Before the Avatar Storm they would just whype the floor with the Awakening Magi with sheer numbers of <u>active archmages</u>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T18:14:53-07:00","id":988035,"title":"","content":"For the record, <b>ManuDomine</b> posted as I was doing mine. And I completely agree about the most probable allyance being &quot;everyone against the Seers&quot;. They will need every meat shield they can muster, just to postpone their complete failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T19:49:27-07:00","id":988071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988030#post988030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6042_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6042\" data-vbnamecard=\"6042\">ManusDomine</a><br /> 1- The terrible battle was <u>at least</u> that powerful, and Doissetep felled anyway;</div> </div> </div> </div>Stilll won't make it canon that it was Doissetep, the Union didn't really draw on their full power during that one either. Though this one isn't really relevant, so I suggest we drop it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988030#post988030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- As I said, yes, they still have a huge power. But believe, the Traditions also have. Both are a lot weakened, but still scary. Though it is impossible to say what side suffered most, it made things more balanced because it is easier to tip the balance now;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh they definitely do possess a lot of power, but well, that power really isn't enough to challenge the Union, like the Revised corebook pretty much clearly sets up this situation where you really can't fight the Union by fighting a war. To fight the Union, you have to play the Union's game, meaning a war of ideas and culture, which the Traditions really aren't that well set up to do.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Virtual Adepts can do it through the internet.<br /> <br /> <i>Maybe.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988030#post988030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Guide to Technocracy directly states that the Union power is far from enough to keep things with such certainty anymore. It also states directly that the Consensus is getting out of control;</div> </div> </div> </div>ATLAS units didn't exist during Guide to The Technocracy, I'm drawing on information primarily from the Revised Conventionbooks where the Union has regained a lot of power and is still alive and kicking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988030#post988030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4- Just for the record, both are still on par with the Awakening and far more used and prepared for war. Before the Avatar Storm they would just whype the floor with the Awakening Magi with sheer numbers of <u>active archmages</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, there is a good reason that I refuse to compare the Technocracy before the Dimensional Anomaly with anything, because the Union before the Avatar Storm was <i>ridiculous</i>. Actually using the Union from before the Anomaly is quickly grounds for hilarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T23:04:13-07:00","id":988145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=987782#post987782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the brute force angle, the Union has ATLAS Units, who will quickly become nightmare fuel in the nWoD. For those who don't know what an ATLAS is, it's basically a mage that has been so broken by NWO torture and brainwashed by Processing that his personality has been reworked completely, the only thing left of him, is basically his brain, everything else is a Primium (read: What Thaumium wishes to be when it grows up) skeleton, plated in even more Primium and equipped with all sorts of nasty weapons, like spike throwers that literally throw people meters and impale them on walls. They can also do magic like a mage while being almost immune to any sort of magic or supernatural abilities, and tanky enough to make an actual tank jealous.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>...the hell? I used to have an encyclopedic grasp of all things WoD, but even tho it's been a while since I went through those old books, I'm pretty sure I never heard of THIS. Is this perhaps something that came about after WW brought the OWoD back? Man, as if HITMarks weren't <i>enough</i>...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On a more basic level: A Tradition Mage and a Pentacle Mage are casting magic spells near each other, and each uses Prime to see what the other is doing. What do they see, exactly?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T23:06:57-07:00","id":988146,"title":"","content":"Mummy meets Mummy: Both are ancient immortals from Egypt (or, something like Egypt) who spend some time in Duat. How might they view each other? Could the Reborn free the Arisen from the Judges? What about the Lifeless and Bane Mummies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T03:06:02-07:00","id":988196,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing about the technocracy: That stranglehold they had on reality in Ascension? It's <i>gone.</i> The consensus in Chronicles is &quot;Monsters are totes real, but I'm not going to talk about it because that's what crazy people do and/or I'd get eaten.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T03:23:20-07:00","id":988198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988145#post988145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...the hell? I used to have an encyclopedic grasp of all things WoD, but even tho it's been a while since I went through those old books, I'm pretty sure I never heard of THIS. Is this perhaps something that came about after WW brought the OWoD back? Man, as if HITMarks weren't <i>enough</i>...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Conventionbook: NWO Revised to be exact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988145#post988145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more basic level: A Tradition Mage and a Pentacle Mage are casting magic spells near each other, and each uses Prime to see what the other is doing. What do they see, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> I have no idea? I must consider this question further...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:03:59-07:00","id":988272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988146#post988146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy meets Mummy: Both are ancient immortals from Egypt (or, something like Egypt) who spend some time in Duat. How might they view each other? Could the Reborn free the Arisen from the Judges? What about the Lifeless and Bane Mummies?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the exact reason I want more Translation guides. Give me a &quot;War of the Judges&quot;, dammit. An eternal shadow war, hidden even from the ancient eyes of the Mummies, a battle between beings beyond god-like for control of the Afterlife, where even the Kings and Queens are merely somebody else's amnesiac pawns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T16:26:43-07:00","id":989067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988145#post988145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more basic level: A Tradition Mage and a Pentacle Mage are casting magic spells near each other, and each uses Prime to see what the other is doing. What do they see, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly an interesting question.<br /> <br /> My theory: Supernal Magic is the imposition of Supernal Realm's rules on this earth, so it should seem like Stactic Spirit effects for Ascension's Mages, but drawing from a distant and powerful Tellurian beyond their grasp (for now). As things go on Ascension, the details remain mostly dependent on the observer, not so much on the observed.<br /> <br /> Paradigm Magic is the imposition of one's own rules on this earth, so it would have one of two effects for Awakening's Mage Sight: or it would seem like bringing power from one's own Oneiros, using your personal take on the Superrnal Symbols, or it would be the even weirder case of a person able to impose its own new Symbols on the Supernal ones (if those were present at all).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988196#post988196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing about the technocracy: That stranglehold they had on reality in Ascension? It's <i>gone.</i> The consensus in Chronicles is &quot;Monsters are totes real, but I'm not going to talk about it because that's what crazy people do and/or I'd get eaten.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is like going against the OP and saying that the setting of the encounter is the CoD by definition. It can as easily be said that the setting is the cWoD, and in this case the Technocracy would be essentially beyond hope for the CoD's Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T16:50:45-07:00","id":989074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=988007#post988007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a side note, one of the scenarios presented in the book Time of Judgment: Ascension is a probable inspiration for Awakening, and maybe for the entire CoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which scenario is this? It's been a long time since I read Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T18:49:03-07:00","id":989122,"title":"","content":"By memory now, I remember that it had something to do initially with aliens, but I'm not sure i those are the same, I also read it a long time ago, I'll take a look soon to give more details. For now, I won't spoil the little I do remember, it is curious enough to be worth a look in the book. The &quot;easter egg&quot; will be almost in the end of the scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T20:25:18-07:00","id":989173,"title":"","content":"Done: the scenario is Chapter Five: A Whimper, Not a Bang. It won't seen to go this way at first, but you will see what I say at least three times in some of the last pages of the chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T01:56:57-07:00","id":989251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989067#post989067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is like going against the OP and saying that the setting of the encounter is the CoD by definition. It can as easily be said that the setting is the cWoD, and in this case the Technocracy would be essentially beyond hope for the CoD's Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The premise was that the two worlds <i>merged</i>. Logically this means that the consensus has been halved in power. I'm not saying the Technocracy is totally fucked, just that it's grip is severely weakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T05:10:29-07:00","id":989297,"title":"","content":"Plus it's not as if they aren't riddled with nephandi and dealing with Threat Null.<br /> <br /> For an unassailable indestructible organization they sure have a lot of groups assailing and destroying them. Even the Atlas units look like they're gearing up to rebel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T08:33:37-07:00","id":989362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989297#post989297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus it's not as if they aren't riddled with nephandi and dealing with Threat Null.<br /> <br /> For an unassailable indestructible organization they sure have a lot of groups assailing and destroying them. Even the Atlas units look like they're gearing up to rebel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I never called them unassailable, please don't put words in my mouth.<br /> <br /> The Union is ridiculously powerful, like absurdly so.<br /> <br /> But in no way unassailable.<br /> <br /> What I did however say, was that they had significantly more hard power to hit people with than what the Seers demonstrate, with the exception of Ochemata.<br /> <br /> The &quot;riddled with Nephandi&quot; thing is something coming from M20, you are free to discuss that, but I am not going to engage with that discussion out of distaste for M20, and preference for a Union that does bad things out of a &quot;to make an omelet, you gotta break a few eggs&quot; logic rather than because they serve space-wizard-satan-cthulu, while Threat Null are explicitly the old Technocracy stuck in the Void, who have been changed into EDEs and thus are able to fight the Union due to possessing the same technology, the same (if not more) knowledge and holding all the control codes.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, to say that the ATLAS units are gearing up to rebel is a bit of a stretch, when what we <i>actually see</i> is that the ATLAS units beat their commander at tactics and Synapse points out that his plan has numerable flaws and that rebellion certainly is a possibility that Smith should consider, which he dismisses with arrogance. When we take a look at the Procedure used to make ATLAS units, we can see that without repeated and constant re-Processing, the threat of rebellion is indeed something that should be considered, but as long as an ATLAS is under Processing, they are in no threat of revolting against the Union.<br /> <br /> But no, the Technocracy is not invincible, no one is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:54:35-07:00","id":989409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989362#post989362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The &quot;riddled with Nephandi&quot; thing is something coming from M20, you are free to discuss that, but I am not going to engage with that discussion out of distaste for M20, and preference for a Union that does bad things out of a &quot;to make an omelet, you gotta break a few eggs&quot; logic rather than because they serve space-wizard-satan-cthulu, while Threat Null are explicitly the old Technocracy stuck in the Void, who have been changed into EDEs and thus are able to fight the Union due to possessing the same technology, the same (if not more) knowledge and holding all the control codes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what's this about the Technocracy serving space-wizard-satan-cthulhu? I haven't yet got my hands on the M20 stuff, so I wasn't aware of all the changes. Did that really happen?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T13:38:28-07:00","id":989511,"title":"","content":"So, is it just me, or is Ascension the most convoluted of the WoD gamelines? Because you guys are really starting to lose me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:16:15-07:00","id":989536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989409#post989409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what's this about the Technocracy serving space-wizard-satan-cthulhu? I haven't yet got my hands on the M20 stuff, so I wasn't aware of all the changes. Did that really happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. There are lots of mentions that the Technocracy may be riddled with Nephandi (in fact, it's a possibiltiy that the Traditions are too). I think a lot of people take that as the 'worshipping the old ones', but that's not actually how M20 portrays what Nephandi are.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic Nephandi aren't dancing around worshiping Cthulhu. They're simply using the power of the Technocracy in a nihilistic manner to predate on humanity. The Nephandi are a mindset, not a paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:49:51-07:00","id":989551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989511#post989511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, is it just me, or is Ascension the most convoluted of the WoD gamelines? Because you guys are really starting to lose me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The basics of Ascension are simple (Traditions VS Technocracy with the Disparates thrown in there), but once you start digging into the deep stuff (Doissetep? Horizon? Deep Umbra?) you run into a setting as complex as its system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:59:44-07:00","id":989558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989251#post989251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The premise was that the two worlds <i>merged</i>. Logically this means that the consensus has been halved in power. I'm not saying the Technocracy is totally fucked, just that it's grip is severely weakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the premise was that the two groups of splats encounter each other in a given way that absolutely no one is lessened in power. So that means that somehow both Technocracy <u>and</u> Seers still have their entire grasp of reallity. It isn't to construct a clear, coherent and complete setting, it is just to make a kind of 'educated' neutral comparison.<br /> <br /> About the 'space-wizard-satan-cthulhu', though <b>Michael</b> is right in saying it isn't a precise description, it isn't an impossible one, either. In a nutshell, maybe a third of the Nephandi should be of the 'cthulhu-cult' kind. Add to that that most Nephandi came from the same Paradigm they &quot;spy&quot; now, it is very likely that most of the Nephandi in the Union (even if they're few there are cetainly some, the same to any other group) are going to be of a primarily Tech Paradigm. It isn't impossible for them to be Wyrm Worshipers or demonologists, but space-wizard-satan-cthulhu seems very likely to most of those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989511#post989511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, is it just me, or is Ascension the most convoluted of the WoD gamelines? Because you guys are really starting to lose me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Believe-me, you saw nothing. Given that the Consensus and some other magic can rewright reallity and retcon and mmnot recon it at the same time, things get really weird in Mage's history. Not to say about how the barrier between Umbra and Material Reallity changes with Consensus and Paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T19:26:14-07:00","id":989668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989558#post989558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the premise was that the two groups of splats encounter each other in a given way that absolutely no one is lessened in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>The premise doesn't state that the groups aren't lessened in power, just that the cosmology remains workable for all monster types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T01:58:59-07:00","id":989781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide#post978575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Opening Premise: ... As improbable as it sounds, this is a stable union, <b><u>that somehow preserves cosmologies that would normally be considered incompatible</u></b> (IOW, this is pure Handwavium, meant to preempt arguments that only one set of Mages' powers should work, etc, which would not be in the spirit of the thread's intent).... is the world big enough for the Seers and the Technocracy?...</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't say it isn't open to interpretation, but for me it is very clear that assuming a lessened Consensus breaks the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:09:04-07:00","id":989783,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I shouldn't have said that the <i>consensus </i>was weakened. The Consensus itself is as strong as ever. It's just ceased to be what the Technocracy wants it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:11:52-07:00","id":989784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989536#post989536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly. There are lots of mentions that the Technocracy may be riddled with Nephandi (in fact, it's a possibiltiy that the Traditions are too). I think a lot of people take that as the 'worshipping the old ones', but that's not actually how M20 portrays what Nephandi are.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic Nephandi aren't dancing around worshiping Cthulhu. They're simply using the power of the Technocracy in a nihilistic manner to predate on humanity. The Nephandi are a mindset, not a paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why not simply say that the Union is filled with people who abuse their power or line their pockets with money and funding that should have gone to helpful stuff instead of calling them Nephandi?<br /> <br /> Because the Nephandi as portrayed are still absolutely the same old Inverted Avatar assholes who murder people for fun and torture puppies because why not. Under the description of Technephandi (God what an awful name) on page 228-229, they are described as having a hold on the Inner Circle. You still have to go through the Cauls and you still get your Avatar inverted and dedicate yourself to oblivion.<br /> <br /> But yes, when I called them worshippers of space-wizard-satan-cthulu, it was mostly for the fun of it honestly, mainly because I think &quot;space-wizard-satan-cthulu&quot; sounds more hilarious than &quot;rape-murder-torture-wizards&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:42:13-07:00","id":989796,"title":"","content":"Given how the Caul works, I find both good descriptions. They are, one way or another, worshippers or servants to some sort of lovecraftian entity, since that is pretty much what Wyrm and Demons are going to be in extreme cases.<br /> <br /> Either way, Nephandi shouldn't be assumed by default as the main force behind any group that doesn't exist for that very purpose in the setting. They should be taken in their own right, but sincerely, I don't see thair status quo changing much in this scenario. The Nefandi and the Scelesti are probably going to do the same as ever, just including the new groups in their endeavors. Alliances and clashes between them would happen in the same way that they already happen between member of the same group, with no pattern whatsoever.<br /> <br /> And as they already are in their respective gamelines, it is up to each ST to define if they are just a little nuisance in the big picture, few in numbers and overarching power, or if they are the evil hidding in every corner and almost all the way ahead on their course to ultimate victory over reallity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:54:42-07:00","id":989802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989784#post989784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why not simply say that the Union is filled with people who abuse their power or line their pockets with money and funding that should have gone to helpful stuff instead of calling them Nephandi?</div> </div> </div> </div>It narratively gives an edge to the corruption of the Technocracy it otherwise wouldn't have. It's one thing to say that the Technocracy are just corrupt, it's another to state that not only are they corrupt but that many of them have actually slipped over into promoting descension.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yes, when I called them worshippers of space-wizard-satan-cthulu, it was mostly for the fun of it honestly, mainly because I think &quot;space-wizard-satan-cthulu&quot; sounds more hilarious than &quot;rape-murder-torture-wizards&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, though I would claim Poe's law applies here.You're going to mislead people as the general view of the Nephandi is traditionally that of space-wizard-satan-Cthulu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T03:13:51-07:00","id":989809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989802#post989802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It narratively gives an edge to the corruption of the Technocracy it otherwise wouldn't have. It's one thing to say that the Technocracy are just corrupt, it's another to state that not only are they corrupt but that many of them have actually slipped over into promoting descension.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't feel like that, I think it cheapens the Union if they're corrupt due to being evil inverted Avatar Nephandi, I would have much preferred it if it was really good at cracking down on Nephandi and had very few of them...<br /> <br /> But when you have a huge group that encourages homogeneity of thought and following orders, you get a lot of people who go &quot;A necessary sacrifice&quot; or &quot;Collateral damage&quot; whenever they kill someone, and that's certainly a very slippery slope.<br /> <br /> But arguing about M20 is probably getting off-topic, so I suggest we cut it off here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989802#post989802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, though I would claim Poe's law applies here.You're going to mislead people as the general view of the Nephandi is traditionally that of space-wizard-satan-Cthulu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T05:24:10-07:00","id":989830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989796#post989796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nefandi and the Scelesti are probably going to do the same as ever, just including the new groups in their endeavors. Alliances and clashes between them would happen in the same way that they already happen between member of the same group, with no pattern whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it's possible to be a scelesti and not devoted to destroying the entire world. Angrboda, for instance, was just after vengeance against a Ministry of Seers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989362#post989362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never called them unassailable, please don't put words in my mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one said unassailable. However between you dismissing the Traditions entirely, deciding to excise weaknesses in the Technocracy and play up their strengths, 'The war against the Union has never been a war,' as well as deciding the ochemata would never come into play. And monteparnas, 'It can as easily be said that the setting is the cWoD, and in this case the Technocracy would be essentially beyond hope for the CoD's Mages.'<br /> <br /> You've described an unassailable organization.<br /> <br /> Are you interested in keeping up the 'versus' vein, a perfectly valid if repetitive concern? Or are you more interested in, as Hand-of-Omega suggested, figuring out ' who has the most impact on the others' culture and how might they grow from here?'<br /> <br /> For instance I could easily see the Technocracy's NWO and Syndicate joining with the Seers, likely becoming their own ministry or in the Syndicate's case joining an existing one. And the Free Council courting most of the Traditions, as they share at least similar outlooks regarding the source of true magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-19-2016, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T06:28:33-07:00","id":989846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989830#post989830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one said unassailable. However between you dismissing the Traditions entirely, deciding to excise weaknesses in the Technocracy and play up their strengths, 'The war against the Union has never been a war,' as well as deciding the ochemata would never come into play. And monteparnas, 'It can as easily be said that the setting is the cWoD, and in this case the Technocracy would be essentially beyond hope for the CoD's Mages.'<br /> <br /> You've described an unassailable organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, here we see the issue.<br /> <br /> We've had something of a misunderstanding here.<br /> <br /> The battle between the Union and the Traditions stopped being a war in about 1800 due to differences in power and scope between the two sides, so you did indeed correct me on that front. I mentioned that Ochemata were irrelevant due to the following factors:<br /> A): Ochemata are rare as shit.<br /> B): Ochemata are not frontline combat units like HITMarks or ATLAS units.<br /> C): Ochemata are still relevant, in the sense that Sauron is still relevant when you fight a band of Uruk-Hai. They are commanders, generals and avatars of the Tyrants, not something that the Seers can deploy willy-nilly.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is unassailable in a direct war, if you want to battle the Union, don't play the game it wants you to play, instead go for the propaganda game and try to convince the Sleepers that you're right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989830#post989830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you interested in keeping up the 'versus' vein, a perfectly valid if repetitive concern?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never been interested in the 'versus' aspect of this debate, though I may have come off as being interested in it.<br /> <br /> I despise versus debates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989830#post989830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or are you more interested in, as Hand-of-Omega suggested, figuring out ' who has the most impact on the others' culture and how might they grow from here?'</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much, more interested in this.<br /> <br /> I think the Traditions will end up taking a lot of inspiration from the Pentacle for example, and structuring their society more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989830#post989830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance I could easily see the Technocracy's NWO and Syndicate joining with the Seers, likely becoming their own ministry or in the Syndicate's case joining an existing one. And the Free Council courting most of the Traditions, as they share at least similar outlooks regarding the source of true magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much cannot.<br /> <br /> The NWO and the Syndicate set the party line for the entire Technocracy, one of them provides funding and controls the economy and the other controls policy and is in charge of Conditioning, they have no reason to leave for the Seers when they are primarily motivated by &quot;protect the Masses and guide humanity&quot;and they already control the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> The Void Engineers however...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:33:49-07:00","id":989952,"title":"","content":"I'm not nearly as familiar with old Mage as new Mage, but isn't time travel in Awakening 2e significantly safer than Ascension? How would that affect the balance of power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:29:08-07:00","id":990138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989830#post989830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it's possible to be a scelesti and not devoted to destroying the entire world. Angrboda, for instance, was just after vengeance against a Ministry of Seers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said they would just keep doing whatever they do, and I'm aware of their variety of agendas, specialy in the Scelesti's case. Nephandi are kinda singleminded...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=989830#post989830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one said unassailable. However between you dismissing the Traditions entirely, deciding to excise weaknesses in the Technocracy and play up their strengths, 'The war against the Union has never been a war,' as well as deciding the ochemata would never come into play. And monteparnas, 'It can as easily be said that the setting is the cWoD, and in this case the Technocracy would be essentially beyond hope for the CoD's Mages.'<br /> <br /> You've described an unassailable organization.<br /> <br /> Are you interested in keeping up the 'versus' vein, a perfectly valid if repetitive concern? Or are you more interested in, as Hand-of-Omega suggested, figuring out ' who has the most impact on the others' culture and how might they grow from here?'<br /> <br /> For instance I could easily see the Technocracy's NWO and Syndicate joining with the Seers, likely becoming their own ministry or in the Syndicate's case joining an existing one. And the Free Council courting most of the Traditions, as they share at least similar outlooks regarding the source of true magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>So many misinterpretations, I won't bother actualy answering.<br /> <br /> But mostly agreed with the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:06:51-07:00","id":991426,"title":"","content":"I cannot see the Technocracy and the Seers of the Throne joining forces. From the Technocracy's perspective, the Seers embody everything that the Union was founded to fight: a mystical elite that seeks to keep humanity divided and weak in the face of their masters, who are by all accounts living symbols of oppression and tyranny. The irony of how similar their own policies are is generally lost on them, and doesn't alter matters to any appreciable extent even when acknowledged. For their part, the Seers have no interest in working with anyone who refuses to bend their knees to the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> OTOH, I could see a referral where Iteration X's Computer turns out to be the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:25:09-07:00","id":991480,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say that some people in the Technocracy won't ally to the Seers, but that's in the same sense some of them ally to the BSD. There are douchbags in the Union who would join forces with the Seers, but for the Union as a whole the Seers are the very thing they swore to protect Humanity against,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T14:06:25-07:00","id":991524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=991480#post991480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say that some people in the Technocracy won't ally to the Seers, but that's in the same sense some of them ally to the BSD. There are douchbags in the Union who would join forces with the Seers, but for the Union as a whole the Seers are the very thing they swore to protect Humanity against,</div> </div> </div> </div>On that same note I can't see the Pentacle teaming up with the Technocracy for the same reason. The policies of the Technocracy support the Lie just as much as the actions of the Seers do. In addition to this, they would be actively eliminating Mysteries for the Awakened to investigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T14:11:41-07:00","id":991526,"title":"","content":"Yes, at a certain point it doesn't matter if they join or not, they're doing the will of the Exarchs regardless. Just like even if the Traditions don't 'team up' with the Pentacle some are still trying to enlighten the world and some of their goals are intertwined. Though like the Pentacle they have their share of Lie-bolstering activities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:10:43-07:00","id":991549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=991526#post991526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, at a certain point it doesn't matter if they join or not, they're doing the will of the Exarchs regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, they're from a different setting after all.<br /> <br /> In CofD they may be puppets of the Exarchs, but that's not really a given since this requires making the CofD cosmology dominant.<br /> <br /> On another note, I could see Pantechnicon joining on with the Union as a propaganda division of NWO, given that &quot;technobabble so hard that no one but the elite understand it&quot; is literally how you make science work in WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T02:36:02-07:00","id":991780,"title":"","content":"I like making Slashers and all Geniuses, Lemurians, low-Obligation and otherwise, immune to Disquiet and the effect the Wasteland has on people. And if their particular kind of SCIENCE matches the Wasteland in question somehow the Genius can revert the damage if they do so desire (Epikrato, Exelixi and Metaptropi come to mind). If the Genius' Unmada field matches the Wasteland the two just cancel each other out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T09:09:29-07:00","id":991868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=991780#post991780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like making Slashers and all Geniuses, Lemurians, low-Obligation and otherwise, immune to Disquiet and the effect the Wasteland has on people. And if their particular kind of SCIENCE matches the Wasteland in question somehow the Genius can revert the damage if they do so desire (Epikrato, Exelixi and Metaptropi come to mind). If the Genius' Unmada field matches the Wasteland the two just cancel each other out.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is this relevant to the topic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:32:06-07:00","id":991950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=991868#post991868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is this relevant to the topic?</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't. At all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=991524#post991524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that same note I can't see the Pentacle teaming up with the Technocracy for the same reason. The policies of the Technocracy support the Lie just as much as the actions of the Seers do. In addition to this, they would be actively eliminating Mysteries for the Awakened to investigate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think of an initial alliance, only. The Technocracy is at odds with the Traditions for very similar reasons they will surely be at odds with the Pentacle, and likewise, the Traditions resist the Union for reasons very similar, if not completely, to that of the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> But the Seers are going to be a common pain in the ass. The Union dislikes &quot;Reallity Deviants&quot; a lot, but a bunch of world dominators are on a superior level (even if they're something very similar to begin with, though not quite the same). Those two groups are a sure clash. From that, Traditions and Pentacle would be able to choose from a lot of possibilities on how to proceed.<br /> <br /> What I think more probable, not in the &quot;more than 50% likely&quot; sense, but in the &quot;greater than any particular possibility of a great number of them&quot; sense, is that the Pentacle will choose sooner or later to ally to the Technocracy, so they can get rid from the Seers and have a group easier to deal with, since they're not interested in fighting for the Consensus. The Traditions are also more prone to choose the side of a known enemy that won't hide the wonders of the world just for personal gain and profit.<br /> <br /> It isn't a simple or easy choice, and I said it is the most complex scenario from all brought by the theme of the thread. The only thing that is a sure is that Tech and Seers aren't going to see in each other's eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:54:47-07:00","id":992032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=991950#post991950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't a simple or easy choice, and I said it is the most complex scenario from all brought by the theme of the thread. The only thing that is a sure is that Tech and Seers aren't going to see in each other's eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only Technocrat eyes that will look upon a Seer's will be the merciless eye of a HITMark before the kill.<br /> <br /> The Pentacle is ideologically closer to the Union in literally every way (hello Silver Ladder, hello Guardians), and not <i>literally the barons taxing the night, that the Order of Reason was set up to fight</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:18:59-07:00","id":992052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=992032#post992032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only Technocrat eyes that will look upon a Seer's will be the merciless eye of a HITMark before the kill.<br /> <br /> The Pentacle is ideologically closer to the Union in literally every way (hello Silver Ladder, hello Guardians), and not <i>literally the barons taxing the night, that the Order of Reason was set up to fight</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that rhyme intentional?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:37:24-07:00","id":992069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=992052#post992052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was that rhyme intentional?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm... *reads it through for rhymes about three times*<br /> <br /> Yes, of course it was!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:18:06-07:00","id":992091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=992032#post992032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only Technocrat eyes that will look upon a Seer's will be the merciless eye of a HITMark before the kill.<br /> <br /> The Pentacle is ideologically closer to the Union in literally every way (hello Silver Ladder, hello Guardians), and not <i>literally the barons taxing the night, that the Order of Reason was set up to fight</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the Union has changed quite a bit from the Order of Reason of old as well. The Pentacle is also not a monolithic entity, so I could see some disagreements between different regions on who to side with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:19:12-07:00","id":992092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=992032#post992032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only Technocrat eyes that will look upon a Seer's will be the merciless eye of a HITMark before the kill.<br /> <br /> The Pentacle is ideologically closer to the Union in literally every way (hello Silver Ladder, hello Guardians), and not <i>literally the barons taxing the night, that the Order of Reason was set up to fight</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nor the Traditions are really the tyrants the Order of Reason was meant to fight.<br /> Things are complex in this scenario, many possibilities, I can't say what's right.<br /> It began to get more confuse way before, in the time of Revised.<br /> For me it is ludicrous to think either one to be just as devised.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I just couldn't resist...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T17:36:03-07:00","id":992123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=992091#post992091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but the Union has changed quite a bit from the Order of Reason of old as well. The Pentacle is also not a monolithic entity, so I could see some disagreements between different regions on who to side with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Union has changed to be even more antagonistic towards Reality Deviants, like look at this:<br /> <br /> -Bring Stasis and order to the Universe. Predictability brings safety. Once all is discovered and all is known, Unity will be won.<br /> -Convince the Masses from the benevolence of science, commerce, politics, and of the power of Rationality. Conflict and suffering will be eliminated in our Utopia.<br /> -Preserve the Gauntlet and the Horizon. Chaotic individuals who open gateways with impunity threaten the stability of our world. Uncontrolled portals also allow outside forces, such as Nephandi, access to our world. This must never happen.<br /> -Define the nature of the universe. Knowledge must be absolute or chaos will envelop all. The elemental forces of the universe must not be left to the caprices of the unknown.<br /> -Destroy Reality Deviants. Their recklessness threatens our security and our progress toward Unity.<br /> -Shepherd the Masses; protect them from themselves and others.<br /> <br /> These are the Precepts of Damian, the fundamental rules on which the Union is built.<br /> <br /> And the commandments of the Seers are in violation of Article 2, 3, 5 and 6.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Precepts get re-interpreted all the time, but theSeers are still in fundamental violation of four of them, while the Pentacle are only in violation of one or two (specifically Article 5 and Article 3), making the Pentacle an ally that is at least as acceptable (if not more so) as the Traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:56:50-07:00","id":992164,"title":"","content":"Well, I could see the Diamond getting into an uneasy alliance, but the Free Council would be <i>pissed</i> at the idea of working with the Technocratic Union. They're servants of the Lie to nearly the extent that the Seers are, even if they're not cognizant of that, and if the Diamond allied themselves with the Union, we could well see a toned-down version of the Great Refusal in response.<br /> <br /> They may have a more benign mission statement, but their goal is still &quot;control humanity and cut them off from magic that they don't control&quot; which sound enough like the Seers at a glance to give the hardcore Libertines pause at the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T19:01:47-07:00","id":992169,"title":"","content":"The Exarchs Will:<br /> <br /> Control Magic.<br /> Divide Humanity.<br /> Destroy the Pentacle.<br /> Enslave the Gods.<br /> Protect Humanity.<br /> Regulate the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T21:00:34-07:00","id":992228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=992123#post992123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Bring Stasis and order to the Universe. Predictability brings safety. Once all is discovered and all is known, Unity will be won.<br /> -Convince the Masses from the benevolence of science, commerce, politics, and of the power of Rationality. Conflict and suffering will be eliminated in our Utopia.<br /> -Preserve the Gauntlet and the Horizon. Chaotic individuals who open gateways with impunity threaten the stability of our world. Uncontrolled portals also allow outside forces, such as Nephandi, access to our world. This must never happen.<br /> -Define the nature of the universe. Knowledge must be absolute or chaos will envelop all. The elemental forces of the universe must not be left to the caprices of the unknown.<br /> -Destroy Reality Deviants. Their recklessness threatens our security and our progress toward Unity.<br /> -Shepherd the Masses; protect them from themselves and others.<br /> <br /> These are the Precepts of Damian, the fundamental rules on which the Union is built.<br /> <br /> And the commandments of the Seers are in violation of Article 2, 3, 5 and 6.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Precepts get re-interpreted all the time, but theSeers are still in fundamental violation of four of them, while the Pentacle are only in violation of one or two (specifically Article 5 and Article 3), making the Pentacle an ally that is at least as acceptable (if not more so) as the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is both beautiful and terrible. As much as I love the Traditions, I love the Technocratic Union.<br /> <br /> Article 1 is somewhat in conflict with the Pentacle and the Free Council, but it doesn't have to be. If their allies in the Union focus on research, it isn't a problem at all.<br /> Article 2, again, depends on interpretation. From an Awakening's Mage POV, it isn't a problem per se, if they can be convinced to let superstition be at least recorded.<br /> Article 3 isn't a problem not even to most Traditions. It is just common sense for someone who wants safety for the world at large, and also means that exploring outer-realms is desirable.<br /> Article 4 isn't just acceptable, it is the very core of preceipts for both Pentacle and Free Council. The Traditions want mystery to remain mysterious. Pentacle and FC want to solve mysteries.<br /> Article 5 is really problematic by default, but is also workable. The point is the definition of Reality Deviant, and this definition can be made to include just people whose &quot;recklessness threatens our security and our progress toward Unity&quot;. It doesn't have to be everyone who believe in something else. The problem with the Traditions comes from how Paradigm works, but it means nothing to the Pentacle or FC.<br /> Article 6 is something the Pentacle already does. The Guardians of the Veil, the Adamantine Arrow and the Silver Ladder already works toward this to some extend.<br /> <br /> Even the Traditions don't enter conflict with such commandments every time. Of course, a lot of conflict occurs because there are Mages who contradict some of them in a regular basis (even inside the Union proper, if to a lesser extend), there are prejudices and extremism on all groups involved, and so on. But the Seers are so clearly against so much of this...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T03:01:26-07:00","id":992308,"title":"","content":"Just an aside, you kept saying &quot;Pentacle and Free Council.&quot; The Pentacle is the collective name for the alliance of the Diamond Orders and the Free Council.<br /> <br /> Also I think the thing about number 4 is that it will have totally opposite effects in the two worlds. In OWoD defining nature calcifies it. It renders any magic save for that which has become science impossible. In Chronicles, by comparison, Nature already has a definition, and doing magic requires becoming aware of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T07:26:15-07:00","id":992375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=992228#post992228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is both beautiful and terrible. As much as I love the Traditions, I love the Technocratic Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, I like the Traditions, but it's the Technocracy I've been running a campaign for since 1999.<br /> <br /> The important thing about the Precepts is that the Inner Circle and various Symposiums reinterpret them to suit their purposes constantly, and there is absolutely no reason to enter a silly, unwinnable four-way war with the Traditions, the Diamond, the Free Council and the Seers when you could instead go &quot;oh well yeah, but according to the <i>spirit</i> of the Precepts we can totally ally with the Pentacle against the Seers amirite gize?&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T17:29:00-07:00","id":992647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978575-when-worlds-of-darkness-collide?p=992308#post992308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just an aside, you kept saying &quot;Pentacle and Free Council.&quot; The Pentacle is the collective name for the alliance of the Diamond Orders and the Free Council.<br /> <br /> Also I think the thing about number 4 is that it will have totally opposite effects in the two worlds. In OWoD defining nature calcifies it. It renders any magic save for that which has become science impossible. In Chronicles, by comparison, Nature already has a definition, and doing magic requires becoming aware of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, on everything. About the number 4, it is really a thing of cWoD vs CoD in general. WoD was created under the Punk ethos, and it is in everything of the setting. The CoD is almost the subversion of said ethos, the reconstruction of the desconstructed society. There is a lot behind that on a philosophycal and sociological level. Like, real matherial for real academic work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}